{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DrpgN7kwgBhmZfWgyK6kQR","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Implementation Plan: Docker Sandbox for Ralph Loops\n     2→\n     3→## Overview\n     4→\n     5→This plan implements Docker-based sandboxing for Ralph loop execution. The sandbox wraps existing loop execution in per-loop Docker containers with credential mounting, isolating agent activity to the project directory. Two execution paths are supported:\n     6→\n     7→- **Claude Code loops**: Claude CLI runs natively inside the container with mounted credentials\n     8→- **OpenCode loops**: `opencode serve` runs on the host; the container calls Vista's proxy endpoint via HTTP\n     9→\n    10→The sandbox is opt-in (`sandbox.enabled` toggle in the dashboard), fully transparent to the MCP tool interface, and degrades gracefully when Docker is unavailable.\n    11→\n    12→### Specs Covered\n    13→\n    14→| Spec | Key Concerns |\n    15→|------|-------------|\n    16→| `settings.md` | `ralph.sandbox` settings schema, defaults, validation |\n    17→| `credential-management.md` | Credential providers, path translation, UID/GID |\n    18→| `access-profiles.md` | Named mount profiles, variable substitution |\n    19→| `container-lifecycle.md` | ContainerManager, OpenCodeServeManager, orphan cleanup |\n    20→| `ralph-mcp-integration.md` | RalphService sandbox branch, loop templates, job metadata |\n    21→| `dashboard-ui.md` | Sandbox toggle, inline Docker status |\n    22→\n    23→### Codebase Context\n    24→\n    25→Current state of key files that will be modified:\n    26→\n    27→- **`vista/server/config.py`** — Has `_RALPH_DEFAULTS`, `get_ralph_settings()`, `save_ralph_settings()`, `_merge_dicts()`. Pattern: defaults dict + merge function + getter/setter.\n    28→- **`vista/server/services/ralph_service.py`** — `RalphService` class with `create_job()` (subprocess.Popen), `stop_job()` (os.kill), `get_job_status()` (PID check + output parsing). Single module-level instance: `ralph_service`.\n    29→- **`vista/portable/ralph.py`** — Contains `LOOP_SCRIPT_TEMPLATE` (PowerShell). Used by both standalone CLI and `RalphService`. Claude invocation in template: `$PromptContent | claude -p --dangerously-skip-permissions --output-format=stream-json --model $Model`.\n    30→- **`vista/server/app.py`** — FastAPI app with lifespan context manager. Startup: ensure paths. Shutdown: stop loops. Routes registered via `app.include_router()`.\n    31→- **`vista/server/routes/ralph_settings.py`** — `GET/PUT /api/settings/ralph` for ralph settings management.\n    32→\n    33→---\n    34→\n    35→## Phase 1: Settings & Data Models\n    36→\n    37→**Goal:** Extend config system with sandbox settings schema and create shared data models. This is the foundation all subsequent phases depend on.\n    38→\n    39→### Step 1.1: Sandbox defaults in `config.py`\n    40→\n    41→**File:** `vista/server/config.py` (modify)\n    42→\n    43→Add `_SANDBOX_DEFAULTS` following the existing pattern of `_RALPH_DEFAULTS`:\n    44→\n    45→```python\n    46→_SANDBOX_DEFAULTS = {\n    47→    \"enabled\": False,\n    48→    \"image\": \"vista-ralph:latest\",\n    49→    \"network\": True,\n    50→    \"opencode_serve\": {\"port\": 4096, \"auto_start\": True},\n    51→    \"credentials\": {\n    52→        \"claude_auth\": True,\n    53→        \"git_ssh\": True,\n    54→        \"git_config\": True,\n    55→        \"github_cli\": False,\n    56→        \"custom\": [],\n    57→    },\n    58→    \"profiles\": {\n    59→        \"full-access\": {\"mounts\": [{\"path\": \".\", \"mode\": \"rw\"}]},\n    60→        \"feature-scoped\": {\"mounts\": [\n    61→            {\"path\": \".vista/features/${FEATURE}\", \"mode\": \"rw\"},\n    62→            {\"path\": \".vista/ralph/${FEATURE}\", \"mode\": \"rw\"},\n    63→            {\"path\": \"src\", \"mode\": \"rw\"},\n    64→            {\"path\": \"tests\", \"mode\": \"rw\"},\n    65→            {\"path\": \".git\", \"mode\": \"rw\"},\n    66→        ]},\n    67→        \"research-only\": {\"mounts\": [{\"path\": \".\", \"mode\": \"ro\"}], \"network\": False},\n    68→    },\n    69→    \"model_defaults\": {},\n    70→}\n    71→```\n    72→\n    73→Add functions (following existing `get_ralph_settings` / `get_ralph_defaults` patterns):\n    74→\n    75→- `get_sandbox_settings() -> dict` — `_merge_dicts(_SANDBOX_DEFAULTS, get_ralph_settings().get(\"sandbox\", {}))`\n    76→- `is_sandbox_enabled() -> bool` — `get_sandbox_settings().get(\"enabled\", False)`\n    77→- `get_sandbox_profile(name: str) -> dict | None` — lookup in `sandbox.profiles`\n    78→- `get_sandbox_credentials() -> dict` — return `sandbox.credentials` section\n    79→- `get_opencode_serve_settings() -> dict` — return `sandbox.opencode_serve` section\n    80→- `save_sandbox_settings(sandbox_config: dict)` — read full settings, set `ralph.sandbox`, write back (same atomic pattern as `save_ralph_settings`)\n    81→\n    82→### Step 1.2: Settings validation\n    83→\n    84→**File:** `vista/server/services/sandbox_settings.py` (new)\n    85→\n    86→Validation functions:\n    87→\n    88→```python\n    89→def validate_sandbox_settings(config: dict) -> list[str]:\n    90→    \"\"\"Return list of validation error strings. Empty = valid.\"\"\"\n    91→```\n    92→\n    93→Rules from the settings spec:\n    94→- `enabled` is bool\n    95→- `image` is non-empty string\n    96→- `network` is bool\n    97→- `opencode_serve.port` is int 1024–65535\n    98→- `opencode_serve.auto_start` is bool\n    99→- Each credential toggle is bool\n   100→- Custom mounts have required fields: `name`, `host_path`, `container_path`\n   101→- Each profile has at least one mount\n   102→- Mount paths relative (no absolute paths, no `..` traversal)\n   103→- Mount modes are `\"rw\"` or `\"ro\"`\n   104→- Profile names match `^[a-z0-9-]+$`\n   105→- `model_defaults` values reference existing profile names\n   106→\n   107→On load: log warnings for invalid fields, apply defaults. On save: reject with errors.\n   108→\n   109→### Step 1.3: Data models\n   110→\n   111→**File:** `vista/server/models/sandbox.py` (new)\n   112→\n   113→```python\n   114→from dataclasses import dataclass, field\n   115→\n   116→@dataclass\n   117→class MountSpec:\n   118→    path: str        # Relative to project root, supports ${FEATURE}\n   119→    mode: str        # \"rw\" or \"ro\"\n   120→\n   121→@dataclass\n   122→class AccessProfile:\n   123→    name: str\n   124→    mounts: list[MountSpec]\n   125→    network: bool | None = None  # None = inherit global\n   126→\n   127→@dataclass\n   128→class CredentialDetection:\n   129→    found: bool\n   130→    method: str           # \"env_var\", \"config_dir\", \"config_file\", \"not_found\"\n   131→    source_path: str\n   132→    display_info: str\n   133→\n   134→@dataclass\n   135→class DockerMount:\n   136→    host_path: str\n   137→    container_path: str\n   138→    mode: str             # \"ro\" or \"rw\"\n   139→\n   140→@dataclass\n   141→class DockerCredentialConfig:\n   142→    env_vars: dict[str, str] = field(default_factory=dict)\n   143→    mounts: list[DockerMount] = field(default_factory=list)\n   144→\n   145→@dataclass\n   146→class ContainerInfo:\n   147→    name: str\n   148→    job_id: str\n   149→    provider: str\n   150→    status: str\n   151→    session_id: str\n   152→```\n   153→\n   154→### Step 1.4: Tests\n   155→\n   156→**File:** `vista/tests/test_sandbox_settings.py` (new)\n   157→\n   158→- Defaults application: missing `sandbox` section, partial section, empty section\n   159→- Validation: invalid modes, missing fields, path traversal (`../../../etc`), port out of range\n   160→- Write-back: preserves existing `ralph.defaults`, `ralph.summarizer`, `server.*`\n   161→- `is_sandbox_enabled()` returns correct bool\n   162→\n   163→---\n   164→\n   165→## Phase 2: Credential Management\n   166→\n   167→**Goal:** Implement credential providers that detect host credentials, generate Docker mount/env configs, and support validation.\n   168→\n   169→### Step 2.1: Path translator\n   170→\n   171→**File:** `vista/server/services/sandbox/path_translator.py` (new)\n   172→\n   173→```python\n   174→class PathTranslator:\n   175→    def translate(self, host_path: str) -> str:\n   176→        \"\"\"Windows: C:\\\\Users\\\\Grove\\\\.ssh → /c/Users/Grove/.ssh\n   177→        Linux/macOS: passthrough\"\"\"\n   178→\n   179→    def get_host_uid_gid(self) -> tuple[int, int]:\n   180→        \"\"\"Windows/WSL2: (1000, 1000). Linux/macOS: os.getuid(), os.getgid()\"\"\"\n   181→```\n   182→\n   183→Implementation:\n   184→- Use `platform.system()` for detection\n   185→- Windows path translation: regex `^([A-Za-z]):\\\\(.*)` → `/$1_lower/$rest_with_forward_slashes`\n   186→- UID/GID: Windows always returns (1000, 1000) since Docker Desktop handles translation. Unix uses `os.getuid()`, `os.getgid()`.\n   187→\n   188→### Step 2.2: Credential providers\n   189→\n   190→**File:** `vista/server/services/sandbox/credential_providers.py` (new)\n   191→\n   192→Base class:\n   193→```python\n   194→class CredentialProvider:\n   195→    name: str\n   196→    display_name: str\n   197→    description: str\n   198→    applies_to: list[str]  # [\"claude\"], [\"*\"], etc.\n   199→\n   200→    def detect(self) -> CredentialDetection: ...\n   201→    def get_docker_config(self) -> DockerCredentialConfig: ...\n   202→    def get_validation_command(self) -> str: ...\n   203→```\n   204→\n   205→Built-in providers:\n   206→\n   207→| Provider | `applies_to` | Detects | Mount | Mode |\n   208→|----------|-------------|---------|-------|------|\n   209→| `ClaudeAuthProvider` | `[\"claude\"]` | `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` env, `~/.claude/` dir | `~/.claude/` → `/home/{user}/.claude/` | **rw** |\n   210→| `GitSshProvider` | `[\"*\"]` | `~/.ssh/` with key files | `~/.ssh/` → `/home/{user}/.ssh/` | ro |\n   211→| `GitConfigProvider` | `[\"*\"]` | `~/.gitconfig` file | `~/.gitconfig` → `/home/{user}/.gitconfig` | ro |\n   212→| `GitHubCliProvider` | `[\"*\"]` | `~/.config/gh/` or `%APPDATA%\\GitHub CLI\\` | → `/home/{user}/.config/gh/` | ro |\n   213→| `CustomMountProvider` | `[\"*\"]` | host_path exists | as specified in settings | as specified |\n   214→\n   215→Gathering function:\n   216→```python\n   217→def gather_credentials(provider_name: str, settings: dict) -> list[DockerCredentialConfig]:\n   218→    \"\"\"Filter by applies_to + settings toggles, detect, return configs.\"\"\"\n   219→```\n   220→\n   221→All providers use `PathTranslator` for host path → Docker path conversion.\n   222→\n   223→### Step 2.3: Tests\n   224→\n   225→**File:** `vista/tests/test_credential_providers.py` (new)\n   226→**File:** `vista/tests/test_path_translator.py` (new)\n   227→\n   228→- Per-provider detection with mocked filesystem (monkeypatch `Path.home()`, `os.environ`)\n   229→- Path translation: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\.ssh` → `/c/Users/Grove/.ssh`\n   230→- Docker config generation: correct mounts and env vars\n   231→- `applies_to` filtering: Claude-only creds skipped for OpenCode loops\n   232→- UID/GID per platform\n   233→- `gather_credentials` end-to-end\n   234→\n   235→---\n   236→\n   237→## Phase 3: Access Profiles\n   238→\n   239→**Goal:** Profile resolution, variable substitution, and Docker mount generation.\n   240→\n   241→Can be developed in parallel with Phase 2 (no interdependency).\n   242→\n   243→### Step 3.1: Profile service\n   244→\n   245→**File:** `vista/server/services/sandbox/access_profiles.py` (new)\n   246→\n   247→```python\n   248→def resolve_profile(\n   249→    explicit: str | None, model: str, settings: dict\n   250→) -> AccessProfile:\n   251→    \"\"\"Priority: explicit override > model_defaults mapping > 'full-access'\"\"\"\n   252→\n   253→def substitute_variables(mount_path: str, feature: str | None) -> str:\n   254→    \"\"\"Replace ${FEATURE} and ${PROJECT_ROOT} in mount paths.\"\"\"\n   255→\n   256→def to_docker_mounts(\n   257→    profile: AccessProfile,\n   258→    project_root: Path,\n   259→    feature: str | None,\n   260→    translator: PathTranslator,\n   261→) -> list[dict]:\n   262→    \"\"\"Convert profile mounts to Docker bind mount specs.\n   263→    Special case: path '.' → mount entire project root as /workspace/\n   264→    Skip non-existent paths with warning (not error).\n   265→    \"\"\"\n   266→\n   267→def validate_profile(profile_dict: dict) -> list[str]:\n   268→    \"\"\"Validate: ≥1 mount, paths relative, no '..', valid modes.\"\"\"\n   269→\n   270→def check_network_compatibility(\n   271→    profile: AccessProfile, provider_name: str, global_network: bool\n   272→) -> None:\n   273→    \"\"\"Raise ValueError if OpenCode + network disabled.\"\"\"\n   274→```\n   275→\n   276→Network policy resolution: `profile.network if profile.network is not None else global_network`\n   277→\n   278→### Step 3.2: Tests\n   279→\n   280→**File:** `vista/tests/test_access_profiles.py` (new)\n   281→\n   282→- Resolution chain: explicit > model_defaults > fallback\n   283→- Variable substitution: `${FEATURE}` → slug, `${PROJECT_ROOT}` → `/workspace`\n   284→- Mount translation: `\".\"` → full project root, relative paths → `/workspace/{path}`\n   285→- Validation: reject `..`, reject absolute paths, require ≥1 mount\n   286→- Network: OpenCode + `network: false` → error with clear message\n   287→- Missing path: skipped with warning\n   288→\n   289→---\n   290→\n   291→## Phase 4: Container Lifecycle Management\n   292→\n   293→**Goal:** Docker container creation, execution, monitoring, teardown, and image management.\n   294→\n   295→### Step 4.1: ContainerManager\n   296→\n   297→**File:** `vista/server/services/sandbox/container_manager.py` (new)\n   298→\n   299→**New dependency:** `docker` Python SDK (`pip install docker`). Import lazily to avoid breaking the plugin when Docker SDK is not installed.\n   300→\n   301→```python\n   302→class ContainerManager:\n   303→    def __init__(self, session_id: str):\n   304→        import docker\n   305→        self.docker = docker.from_env()\n   306→        self.session_id = session_id\n   307→\n   308→    async def create_loop_container(\n   309→        self,\n   310→        job_id: str,\n   311→        provider_name: str,\n   312→        project_root: Path,\n   313→        profile_mounts: list[dict],\n   314→        credentials: list[DockerCredentialConfig],\n   315→        image: str,\n   316→        network: bool = True,\n   317→        env_extra: dict | None = None,\n   318→    ) -> ContainerInfo:\n   319→        \"\"\"\n   320→        1. Combine profile_mounts + credential mounts\n   321→        2. Combine credential env_vars + env_extra + DEVCONTAINER=true\n   322→        3. docker.containers.create() with labels, user, extra_hosts\n   323→        4. container.start()\n   324→        \"\"\"\n   325→\n   326→    async def exec_in_container(\n   327→        self,\n   328→        container_name: str,\n   329→        command: list[str],\n   330→        workdir: str = \"/workspace\",\n   331→        env: dict | None = None,\n   332→        stdout_handle=None,\n   333→    ) -> int:  # returns host PID\n   334→        \"\"\"docker exec — run command inside running container.\"\"\"\n   335→\n   336→    async def remove_container(self, container_name: str) -> None:\n   337→        \"\"\"Stop (timeout=10) + remove container.\"\"\"\n   338→\n   339→    async def cleanup_orphans(self) -> list[str]:\n   340→        \"\"\"Find containers with managed-by=vista-ralph where\n   341→        vista-session != self.session_id. Stop + remove. Return names.\"\"\"\n   342→\n   343→    async def shutdown_all(self) -> None:\n   344→        \"\"\"Stop + remove all containers with managed-by=vista-ralph\n   345→        AND vista-session == self.session_id.\"\"\"\n   346→\n   347→    def list_containers(self) -> list[ContainerInfo]:\n   348→        \"\"\"List all managed containers with status.\"\"\"\n   349→\n   350→    def is_docker_available(self) -> tuple[bool, str]:\n   351→        \"\"\"Try docker.ping(). Return (True, \"Docker running\") or (False, reason).\"\"\"\n   352→\n   353→    async def ensure_image(self, image_name: str = \"vista-ralph:latest\") -> str:\n   354→        \"\"\"Check if image exists locally. If not, build from bundled Dockerfile.\n   355→        Store Dockerfile hash to detect changes.\"\"\"\n   356→```\n   357→\n   358→Container creation details (from container-lifecycle spec):\n   359→- Name: `vista-ralph-{job_id[:8]}`\n   360→- Labels: `managed-by=vista-ralph`, `vista-job-id={job_id}`, `vista-provider={provider}`, `vista-session={session_id}`, `vista-project={hash(project_root)[:8]}`\n   361→- Command: `sleep infinity` (keeps container alive for exec)\n   362→- `extra_hosts={\"host.docker.internal\": \"host-gateway\"}` (Linux compatibility)\n   363→- `user=f\"{uid}:{gid}\"`\n   364→- `working_dir=\"/workspace\"`\n   365→- `network_mode=\"bridge\" if network else \"none\"`\n   366→\n   367→### Step 4.2: Docker image\n   368→\n   369→**File:** `vista/docker/Dockerfile` (new)\n   370→\n   371→Based on claudebox reference (`reference/claudebox/build/Dockerfile`) with simplifications:\n   372→\n   373→- Base: `debian:bookworm`\n   374→- Build args: `USER_ID`, `GROUP_ID`, `NODE_VERSION`\n   375→- Install: git, node (via nvm), claude-code CLI, python3, uv, gh CLI, jq, curl, bash\n   376→- User creation with UID/GID matching\n   377→- `DEVCONTAINER=true`\n   378→- `WORKDIR /workspace`\n   379→- Remove: zsh/fzf customization, tmux config, delta, firewall scripts, entrypoint scripts\n   380→- Simple entrypoint: just `sleep infinity` (Vista uses `docker exec`)\n   381→\n   382→**File:** `vista/docker/.dockerignore` (new)\n   383→\n   384→### Step 4.3: Tests\n   385→\n   386→**File:** `vista/tests/test_container_manager.py` (new)\n   387→\n   388→- Container naming and label generation (unit, no Docker)\n   389→- Volume mount construction from profile + credentials (unit)\n   390→- Docker availability check (mock docker client)\n   391→- Create → exec → remove flow (mock docker client)\n   392→- Orphan cleanup: mock containers from \"old session\" are removed, current session containers preserved\n   393→\n   394→---\n   395→\n   396→## Phase 5: OpenCode Serve Management & Proxy\n   397→\n   398→**Goal:** Host-side `opencode serve` process management and Vista proxy endpoint.\n   399→\n   400→### Step 5.1: OpenCodeServeManager\n   401→\n   402→**File:** `vista/server/services/sandbox/opencode_serve_manager.py` (new)\n   403→\n   404→```python\n   405→class OpenCodeServeManager:\n   406→    def __init__(self, port: int = 4096):\n   407→        self.port = port\n   408→        self.process: subprocess.Popen | None = None\n   409→        self.sessions: dict[str, str] = {}  # job_id → session_id\n   410→\n   411→    async def ensure_running(self) -> None:\n   412→        \"\"\"Start 'opencode serve --port {port} --hostname 127.0.0.1'\n   413→        if not running. Health check: GET http://localhost:{port}/doc\"\"\"\n   414→\n   415→    async def create_session(self, job_id: str, cwd: str) -> str:\n   416→        \"\"\"POST to opencode serve to create session. Return session_id.\"\"\"\n   417→\n   418→    async def close_session(self, job_id: str) -> None:\n   419→        \"\"\"Close session. Remove from self.sessions.\"\"\"\n   420→\n   421→    async def stop(self) -> None:\n   422→        \"\"\"Terminate opencode serve process.\"\"\"\n   423→\n   424→    def is_running(self) -> bool:\n   425→        \"\"\"Process alive + health check passes.\"\"\"\n   426→```\n   427→\n   428→### Step 5.2: Sandbox API routes\n   429→\n   430→**File:** `vista/server/routes/sandbox.py` (new)\n   431→\n   432→```python\n   433→router = APIRouter(prefix=\"/api/sandbox\", tags=[\"sandbox\"])\n   434→\n   435→@router.post(\"/opencode/{session_id}/message\")\n   436→async def opencode_proxy_message(session_id: str, request: Request):\n   437→    \"\"\"Forward message from container to opencode serve on host.\n   438→    1. Validate session_id exists\n   439→    2. Forward request body to http://localhost:{port}/...\n   440→    3. Stream response back to caller\n   441→    \"\"\"\n   442→\n   443→@router.get(\"/status\")\n   444→async def sandbox_status():\n   445→    \"\"\"Returns { docker_available, docker_running, image_built, image_name }\"\"\"\n   446→\n   447→@router.put(\"/settings\")\n   448→async def update_sandbox_settings(body: dict):\n   449→    \"\"\"Toggle sandbox.enabled. Writes to settings.json.\"\"\"\n   450→\n   451→@router.post(\"/credentials/validate\")\n   452→async def validate_credentials():\n   453→    \"\"\"Spin up temp container, run validation commands, tear down.\"\"\"\n   454→\n   455→@router.post(\"/image/build\")\n   456→async def build_image():\n   457→    \"\"\"Trigger sandbox image rebuild.\"\"\"\n   458→```\n   459→\n   460→### Step 5.3: Tests\n   461→\n   462→**File:** `vista/tests/test_opencode_serve_manager.py` (new)\n   463→\n   464→- `ensure_running` with mock subprocess\n   465→- Session create/close with mock HTTP\n   466→- Health check logic\n   467→- Process lifecycle\n   468→\n   469→**File:** `vista/tests/test_sandbox_api.py` (new)\n   470→\n   471→- `GET /api/sandbox/status` returns correct Docker/image state\n   472→- `PUT /api/sandbox/settings` with enabled true/false\n   473→- Proxy endpoint forwards correctly (mock opencode serve)\n   474→\n   475→---\n   476→\n   477→## Phase 6: RalphService Integration\n   478→\n   479→**Goal:** Add sandbox branch to `RalphService` so `create_job()` routes through Docker when enabled. This is the core integration point.\n   480→\n   481→### Step 6.1: Sandbox branch in `create_job()`\n   482→\n   483→**File:** `vista/server/services/ralph_service.py` (modify)\n   484→\n   485→Add at the top of `create_job()`:\n   486→\n   487→```python\n   488→sandbox_settings = config.get_sandbox_settings()\n   489→if sandbox_settings.get(\"enabled\"):\n   490→    return self._create_sandbox_job(\n   491→        job_dir, project_root, slug, mode, task_description,\n   492→        provider, model, iterations, sandbox_settings, job_id\n   493→    )\n   494→# else: existing local subprocess code stays unchanged\n   495→```\n   496→\n   497→**New method `_create_sandbox_job()` (Claude Code path):**\n   498→\n   499→1. Generate `loop.sh` (always bash — container is Linux)\n   500→   - Use existing `LOOP_SCRIPT_TEMPLATE` content but get invocation via `provider.get_invocation(\"sh\")`\n   501→   - The Claude invocation block already supports bash: `printf \"%s\" \"$PROMPT_CONTENT\" | claude -p ...`\n   502→2. Resolve access profile: `resolve_profile(explicit=None, model=model, settings=sandbox_settings)`\n   503→3. Convert profile to Docker mounts: `to_docker_mounts(profile, project_root, slug, translator)`\n   504→4. Gather credentials: `gather_credentials(\"claude\", sandbox_settings)`\n   505→5. Check network compatibility\n   506→6. `container_manager.create_loop_container(job_id, \"claude\", project_root, profile_mounts, credentials, image, network)`\n   507→7. `pid = container_manager.exec_in_container(container_name, [\"bash\", f\"/workspace/.vista/ralph/{slug}-{job_id[:8]}/loop.sh\"], stdout_handle=output_log)`\n   508→8. Save job.json with: `sandbox: True, container: \"vista-ralph-{job_id[:8]}\", pid: exec_pid`\n   509→\n   510→**New method `_create_sandbox_job()` (OpenCode path):**\n   511→\n   512→Same as Claude but additionally:\n   513→1. `opencode_serve_manager.ensure_running()`\n   514→2. `session_id = opencode_serve_manager.create_session(job_id, str(project_root))`\n   515→3. Generate `loop.sh` from **new** `OPENCODE_SANDBOX_LOOP_TEMPLATE`\n   516→4. Gather credentials: `gather_credentials(\"opencode\", sandbox_settings)` — no AI creds\n   517→5. Exec with extra env: `VISTA_HOST=host.docker.internal, VISTA_PORT={port}, OPENCODE_SESSION={session_id}, MODEL={model}`\n   518→6. Save job.json with additional `opencode_session` field\n   519→\n   520→### Step 6.2: OpenCode sandbox loop template\n   521→\n   522→**File:** `vista/portable/ralph.py` (modify — add constant)\n   523→\n   524→Add `OPENCODE_SANDBOX_LOOP_TEMPLATE` — a bash script that:\n   525→- Reads PROMPT + task.md + progress.txt (same compose logic as current template)\n   526→- Uses `curl -s -X POST \"$VISTA_API/message\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d ...` to call Vista proxy\n   527→- Pushes via git after each iteration\n   528→- Checks completion markers (`ALL PHASES COMPLETE`, `Reached max iterations`)\n   529→- Variables: `VISTA_HOST`, `VISTA_PORT`, `OPENCODE_SESSION`, `MODEL` from env\n   530→\n   531→Full template content is in the ralph-mcp-integration spec (lines 95-185).\n   532→\n   533→### Step 6.3: Modify `stop_job()`\n   534→\n   535→**File:** `vista/server/services/ralph_service.py` (modify)\n   536→\n   537→```python\n   538→def stop_job(self, project_root, job_id):\n   539→    # ... load job ...\n   540→    if job.get(\"sandbox\"):\n   541→        self._kill_pid(job[\"pid\"])  # Kill exec process\n   542→        if job.get(\"opencode_session\"):\n   543→            await opencode_serve_manager.close_session(job_id)\n   544→        await container_manager.remove_container(f\"vista-ralph-{job_id[:8]}\")\n   545→    else:\n   546→        # Current behavior unchanged\n   547→```\n   548→\n   549→### Step 6.4: Modify `get_job_status()`\n   550→\n   551→**File:** `vista/server/services/ralph_service.py` (modify)\n   552→\n   553→When `job.get(\"sandbox\")` and PID is not running:\n   554→- Also check if container still exists (container_manager.list_containers)\n   555→- If container gone + PID gone: apply existing completion detection logic\n   556→\n   557→### Step 6.5: Job metadata extension\n   558→\n   559→When sandbox active, `job.json` includes:\n   560→```json\n   561→{\n   562→  \"sandbox\": true,\n   563→  \"container\": \"vista-ralph-{job_id[:8]}\",\n   564→  \"opencode_session\": \"sess_xyz\"  // OpenCode only\n   565→}\n   566→```\n   567→\n   568→When sandbox disabled: `sandbox` key absent (backward compatible).\n   569→\n   570→### Step 6.6: Tests\n   571→\n   572→**File:** `vista/tests/test_ralph_service.py` (modify — add test cases)\n   573→\n   574→- `create_job()` routes to ContainerManager when `sandbox.enabled = true`\n   575→- `create_job()` uses local subprocess when `sandbox.enabled = false`\n   576→- Claude loops generate bash `loop.sh` with native `claude -p`\n   577→- OpenCode loops generate bash `loop.sh` with `curl` calls\n   578→- `job.json` includes `sandbox`, `container`, `opencode_session` when active\n   579→- `stop_job()` kills PID + removes container + closes session\n   580→\n   581→---\n   582→\n   583→## Phase 7: App Lifecycle Integration\n   584→\n   585→**Goal:** Wire sandbox managers into Vista's startup/shutdown and register routes.\n   586→\n   587→### Step 7.1: Sandbox initialization module\n   588→\n   589→**File:** `vista/server/services/sandbox/__init__.py` (modify to add global accessors)\n   590→\n   591→```python\n   592→_container_manager: ContainerManager | None = None\n   593→_opencode_serve_manager: OpenCodeServeManager | None = None\n   594→\n   595→async def init_sandbox() -> None:\n   596→    \"\"\"Called during app startup. Initializes managers if sandbox enabled.\"\"\"\n   597→    global _container_manager, _opencode_serve_manager\n   598→    if not config.is_sandbox_enabled():\n   599→        return\n   600→    session_id = str(uuid4())\n   601→    try:\n   602→        _container_manager = ContainerManager(session_id)\n   603→        orphans = await _container_manager.cleanup_orphans()\n   604→        if orphans:\n   605→            logger.info(f\"Cleaned up {len(orphans)} orphaned containers: {orphans}\")\n   606→        await _container_manager.ensure_image()\n   607→    except Exception as e:\n   608→        logger.error(f\"Sandbox init failed: {e}. Sandbox will be unavailable.\")\n   609→        _container_manager = None\n   610→    serve_settings = config.get_opencode_serve_settings()\n   611→    _opencode_serve_manager = OpenCodeServeManager(serve_settings[\"port\"])\n   612→\n   613→async def shutdown_sandbox() -> None:\n   614→    \"\"\"Called during app shutdown.\"\"\"\n   615→    if _container_manager:\n   616→        await _container_manager.shutdown_all()\n   617→    if _opencode_serve_manager:\n   618→        await _opencode_serve_manager.stop()\n   619→\n   620→def get_container_manager() -> ContainerManager | None:\n   621→    return _container_manager\n   622→\n   623→def get_opencode_serve_manager() -> OpenCodeServeManager | None:\n   624→    return _opencode_serve_manager\n   625→```\n   626→\n   627→### Step 7.2: Modify app lifespan\n   628→\n   629→**File:** `vista/server/app.py` (modify)\n   630→\n   631→```python\n   632→@asynccontextmanager\n   633→async def lifespan(app: FastAPI):\n   634→    config.ensure_full_path()\n   635→    config.DATA_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n   636→    (config.DATA_DIR / \"sessions\").mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n   637→    # NEW: sandbox initialization\n   638→    from server.services.sandbox import init_sandbox, shutdown_sandbox\n   639→    await init_sandbox()\n   640→    yield\n   641→    await loop_service.stop_all()\n   642→    await diagram_watcher.stop()\n   643→    keepalive_manager.stop_all()\n   644→    # NEW: sandbox shutdown\n   645→    await shutdown_sandbox()\n   646→```\n   647→\n   648→Register sandbox routes:\n   649→```python\n   650→from server.routes import sandbox\n   651→app.include_router(sandbox.router)\n   652→```\n   653→\n   654→### Step 7.3: Credential validation at startup\n   655→\n   656→Inside `init_sandbox()`, after image is ensured:\n   657→- Run `validate_credentials()` — creates temp container, runs validation commands per enabled provider\n   658→- Log results (pass/fail per credential) to server output\n   659→- Non-blocking: validation failures are warnings, not startup failures\n   660→\n   661→---\n   662→\n   663→## Phase 8: Dashboard UI\n   664→\n   665→**Goal:** Single toggle + inline Docker status in Ralph settings page.\n   666→\n   667→### Step 8.1: Frontend\n   668→\n   669→**File:** `vista/server/views/ralph_settings.html` (modify)\n   670→\n   671→Add \"Docker Sandbox\" section after existing ralph settings controls:\n   672→\n   673→```\n   674→Docker Sandbox  [toggle: OFF/ON]   {inline status text}\n   675→```\n   676→\n   677→Behavior:\n   678→- Toggle reads/writes `sandbox.enabled` via `PUT /api/sandbox/settings`\n   679→- When toggled ON: call `GET /api/sandbox/status`, display status:\n   680→  - Green dot + \"Docker running\" (available + image built)\n   681→  - Amber dot + \"Building image...\" (available + image building)\n   682→  - Red dot + \"Docker not running\" (installed but stopped)\n   683→  - Red dot + \"Docker Desktop required\" (not installed)\n   684→- When toggled OFF: hide status text\n   685→- Status checked on page load (if ON) and on toggle change\n   686→- No polling — manual refresh\n   687→\n   688→### Step 8.2: Tests\n   689→\n   690→**File:** `vista/tests/test_sandbox_api.py` (extend from Phase 5.3)\n   691→\n   692→- `GET /api/sandbox/status` returns correct states\n   693→- `PUT /api/sandbox/settings` toggles correctly\n   694→- Error states display actionable guidance\n   695→\n   696→---\n   697→\n   698→## Phase 9: Integration Testing\n   699→\n   700→**File:** `vista/tests/integration/test_sandbox_lifecycle.py` (new)\n   701→\n   702→Requires Docker to be installed and running:\n   703→\n   704→- Full `ralph_start → ralph_status → ralph_stop` with sandbox (Claude path)\n   705→- Full cycle with sandbox (OpenCode path via serve proxy)\n   706→- `ralph_summary` reads artifacts produced inside container\n   707→- Orphan cleanup across Vista restarts\n   708→- Concurrent loops in separate containers\n   709→- Bypass mode: `sandbox.enabled = false` runs identically to pre-sandbox\n   710→- Agent can access `.vista/features/`, source code, `.git/` from inside container\n   711→- Agent can `git push` from inside container (SSH keys mounted)\n   712→\n   713→---\n   714→\n   715→## File Summary\n   716→\n   717→### New Files (17)\n   718→\n   719→| File | Phase | Purpose |\n   720→|------|-------|---------|\n   721→| `vista/server/models/sandbox.py` | 1 | Data models (MountSpec, AccessProfile, DockerMount, etc.) |\n   722→| `vista/server/services/sandbox_settings.py` | 1 | Settings validation |\n   723→| `vista/server/services/sandbox/__init__.py` | 2+ | Package init + global accessors + init/shutdown |\n   724→| `vista/server/services/sandbox/path_translator.py` | 2 | Host→Docker path conversion + UID/GID |\n   725→| `vista/server/services/sandbox/credential_providers.py` | 2 | 5 credential providers + gathering |\n   726→| `vista/server/services/sandbox/access_profiles.py` | 3 | Profile resolution, variable substitution, mount translation |\n   727→| `vista/server/services/sandbox/container_manager.py` | 4 | Container lifecycle (create, exec, remove, cleanup, image) |\n   728→| `vista/server/services/sandbox/opencode_serve_manager.py` | 5 | Host-side `opencode serve` management |\n   729→| `vista/server/routes/sandbox.py` | 5 | API endpoints (status, settings, proxy, validate, build) |\n   730→| `vista/docker/Dockerfile` | 4 | Modified claudebox image for Vista sandbox |\n   731→| `vista/docker/.dockerignore` | 4 | Build context ignore |\n   732→| `vista/tests/test_sandbox_settings.py` | 1 | Settings tests |\n   733→| `vista/tests/test_path_translator.py` | 2 | Path translation tests |\n   734→| `vista/tests/test_credential_providers.py` | 2 | Credential provider tests |\n   735→| `vista/tests/test_access_profiles.py` | 3 | Access profile tests |\n   736→| `vista/tests/test_container_manager.py` | 4 | Container lifecycle tests |\n   737→| `vista/tests/test_opencode_serve_manager.py` | 5 | OpenCode serve tests |\n   738→\n   739→### Modified Files (5)\n   740→\n   741→| File | Phase | Changes |\n   742→|------|-------|---------|\n   743→| `vista/server/config.py` | 1 | Add `_SANDBOX_DEFAULTS` + getter/setter functions |\n   744→| `vista/server/services/ralph_service.py` | 6 | Sandbox branch in `create_job()`, `stop_job()`, `get_job_status()` |\n   745→| `vista/portable/ralph.py` | 6 | Add `OPENCODE_SANDBOX_LOOP_TEMPLATE` |\n   746→| `vista/server/app.py` | 7 | Lifespan: init/shutdown sandbox. Register sandbox routes. |\n   747→| `vista/server/views/ralph_settings.html` | 8 | Sandbox toggle + inline Docker status |\n   748→\n   749→### New Dependencies\n   750→\n   751→| Package | Purpose | Install |\n   752→|---------|---------|---------|\n   753→| `docker` | Python Docker SDK for container management | `pip install docker` |\n   754→\n   755→Import lazily — if not installed, sandbox features disabled with clear error. Plugin still functions for non-sandbox usage.\n   756→\n   757→---\n   758→\n   759→## Build Order\n   760→\n   761→```\n   762→Phase 1 (Settings + Models)         ← Foundation\n   763→  ↓\n   764→Phase 2 (Credentials) ─────┐\n   765→Phase 3 (Access Profiles) ──┤       ← Parallel (no interdependency)\n   766→  ↓                         ↓\n   767→Phase 4 (ContainerManager)          ← Core infrastructure\n   768→  ↓\n   769→Phase 5 (OpenCode Serve + API)      ← Second execution path\n   770→  ↓\n   771→Phase 6 (RalphService Integration)  ← Ties everything together\n   772→  ↓\n   773→Phase 7 (App Lifecycle)             ← Startup/shutdown wiring\n   774→  ↓\n   775→Phase 8 (Dashboard UI) ────┐\n   776→Phase 9 (Integration Tests) ┤      ← Parallel (independent)\n   777→```\n   778→\n   779→---\n   780→\n   781→## Spec Alignment Matrix\n   782→\n   783→| Domain Requirement | Implementing Spec | Phase |\n   784→|---|---|---|\n   785→| Prevent file access outside project | access-profiles (container isolation) | 3, 4 |\n   786→| Eliminate credential complexity for OpenCode | credential-management (host-side serve) | 2, 5 |\n   787→| Claudebox as base image | container-lifecycle | 4 |\n   788→| Transparent sandbox (no MCP changes) | ralph-mcp-integration | 6 |\n   789→| Agent access to feature specs | access-profiles (\"full-access\" default) | 3 |\n   790→| Full bypass when disabled | settings, ralph-mcp-integration | 1, 6 |\n   791→| Container-per-loop isolation | container-lifecycle | 4 |\n   792→| Orphan cleanup on startup | container-lifecycle | 7 |\n   793→| Single dashboard toggle | dashboard-ui | 8 |\n   794→| Zero Docker knowledge required | dashboard-ui, settings | 1, 8 |\n   795→| Credential auto-detection | credential-management | 2 |\n   796→| Credential validation at startup | credential-management | 7 |\n   797→| OpenCode serve management | container-lifecycle | 5 |\n   798→| Vista proxy for OpenCode | ralph-mcp-integration | 5 |\n   799→| Path translation (Windows→Docker) | credential-management | 2 |\n   800→| UID/GID matching | credential-management | 2 |\n   801→| Docker availability check | dashboard-ui, container-lifecycle | 4, 8 |\n   802→| Settings validation | settings | 1 |\n   803→| No changes to MCP tool interface | ralph-mcp-integration | 6 (transparent) |\n   804→\n   805→---\n   806→\n   807→## Risk Mitigation\n   808→\n   809→| Risk | Mitigation |\n   810→|---|---|\n   811→| Docker not installed | Lazy import of `docker` SDK. Sandbox marked unavailable. Loops run locally. |\n   812→| Docker not running | `is_docker_available()` check. Dashboard shows actionable guidance. |\n   813→| WSL2 bind mount performance | Acceptable per NFR. Document in known limitations. |\n   814→| Port conflict for opencode serve | Log error, try next available port. |\n   815→| Concurrent loops git conflicts | Documented: separate containers, shared files. Users should use separate branches. |\n   816→| Orphaned containers after crash | Session-based cleanup on every Vista startup. |\n   817→| UID/GID mismatch | Host UID/GID as build args. Windows defaults to 1000:1000. |\n   818→| `~/.claude/` must be rw | Explicitly mounted read-write (differs from claudebox copy pattern). |\n   819→| SSH agent forwarding | Not supported in v1. Only file-based SSH keys. Documented. |\n   820→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b3360bf-9ca7-4816-8cf1-455a270dc126","uuid":"76bb6a7c-9892-44a1-8345-2370ed591fda","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista/.vista/features/docker-sandbox/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md","content":"# Implementation Plan: Docker Sandbox for Ralph Loops\n\n## Overview\n\nThis plan implements Docker-based sandboxing for Ralph loop execution. The sandbox wraps existing loop execution in per-loop Docker containers with credential mounting, isolating agent activity to the project directory. Two execution paths are supported:\n\n- **Claude Code loops**: Claude CLI runs natively inside the container with mounted credentials\n- **OpenCode loops**: `opencode serve` runs on the host; the container calls Vista's proxy endpoint via HTTP\n\nThe sandbox is opt-in (`sandbox.enabled` toggle in the dashboard), fully transparent to the MCP tool interface, and degrades gracefully when Docker is unavailable.\n\n### Specs Covered\n\n| Spec | Key Concerns |\n|------|-------------|\n| `settings.md` | `ralph.sandbox` settings schema, defaults, validation |\n| `credential-management.md` | Credential providers, path translation, UID/GID |\n| `access-profiles.md` | Named mount profiles, variable substitution |\n| `container-lifecycle.md` | ContainerManager, OpenCodeServeManager, orphan cleanup |\n| `ralph-mcp-integration.md` | RalphService sandbox branch, loop templates, job metadata |\n| `dashboard-ui.md` | Sandbox toggle, inline Docker status |\n\n### Codebase Context\n\nCurrent state of key files that will be modified:\n\n- **`vista/server/config.py`** — Has `_RALPH_DEFAULTS`, `get_ralph_settings()`, `save_ralph_settings()`, `_merge_dicts()`. Pattern: defaults dict + merge function + getter/setter.\n- **`vista/server/services/ralph_service.py`** — `RalphService` class with `create_job()` (subprocess.Popen), `stop_job()` (os.kill), `get_job_status()` (PID check + output parsing). Single module-level instance: `ralph_service`.\n- **`vista/portable/ralph.py`** — Contains `LOOP_SCRIPT_TEMPLATE` (PowerShell). Used by both standalone CLI and `RalphService`. Claude invocation in template: `$PromptContent | claude -p --dangerously-skip-permissions --output-format=stream-json --model $Model`.\n- **`vista/server/app.py`** — FastAPI app with lifespan context manager. Startup: ensure paths. Shutdown: stop loops. Routes registered via `app.include_router()`.\n- **`vista/server/routes/ralph_settings.py`** — `GET/PUT /api/settings/ralph` for ralph settings management.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Settings & Data Models\n\n**Goal:** Extend config system with sandbox settings schema and create shared data models. This is the foundation all subsequent phases depend on.\n\n### Step 1.1: Sandbox defaults in `config.py`\n\n**File:** `vista/server/config.py` (modify)\n\nAdd `_SANDBOX_DEFAULTS` following the existing pattern of `_RALPH_DEFAULTS`:\n\n```python\n_SANDBOX_DEFAULTS = {\n    \"enabled\": False,\n    \"image\": \"vista-ralph:latest\",\n    \"network\": True,\n    \"opencode_serve\": {\"port\": 4096, \"auto_start\": True},\n    \"credentials\": {\n        \"claude_auth\": True,\n        \"git_ssh\": True,\n        \"git_config\": True,\n        \"github_cli\": False,\n        \"custom\": [],\n    },\n    \"profiles\": {\n        \"full-access\": {\"mounts\": [{\"path\": \".\", \"mode\": \"rw\"}]},\n        \"feature-scoped\": {\"mounts\": [\n            {\"path\": \".vista/features/${FEATURE}\", \"mode\": \"rw\"},\n            {\"path\": \".vista/ralph/${FEATURE}\", \"mode\": \"rw\"},\n            {\"path\": \"src\", \"mode\": \"rw\"},\n            {\"path\": \"tests\", \"mode\": \"rw\"},\n            {\"path\": \".git\", \"mode\": \"rw\"},\n        ]},\n        \"research-only\": {\"mounts\": [{\"path\": \".\", \"mode\": \"ro\"}], \"network\": False},\n    },\n    \"model_defaults\": {},\n}\n```\n\nAdd functions (following existing `get_ralph_settings` / `get_ralph_defaults` patterns):\n\n- `get_sandbox_settings() -> dict` — `_merge_dicts(_SANDBOX_DEFAULTS, get_ralph_settings().get(\"sandbox\", {}))`\n- `is_sandbox_enabled() -> bool` — `get_sandbox_settings().get(\"enabled\", False)`\n- `get_sandbox_profile(name: str) -> dict | None` — lookup in `sandbox.profiles`\n- `get_sandbox_credentials() -> dict` — return `sandbox.credentials` section\n- `get_opencode_serve_settings() -> dict` — return `sandbox.opencode_serve` section\n- `save_sandbox_settings(sandbox_config: dict)` — read full settings, set `ralph.sandbox`, write back (same atomic pattern as `save_ralph_settings`)\n\n### Step 1.2: Settings validation\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/sandbox_settings.py` (new)\n\nValidation functions:\n\n```python\ndef validate_sandbox_settings(config: dict) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"Return list of validation error strings. Empty = valid.\"\"\"\n```\n\nRules from the settings spec:\n- `enabled` is bool\n- `image` is non-empty string\n- `network` is bool\n- `opencode_serve.port` is int 1024–65535\n- `opencode_serve.auto_start` is bool\n- Each credential toggle is bool\n- Custom mounts have required fields: `name`, `host_path`, `container_path`\n- Each profile has at least one mount\n- Mount paths relative (no absolute paths, no `..` traversal)\n- Mount modes are `\"rw\"` or `\"ro\"`\n- Profile names match `^[a-z0-9-]+$`\n- `model_defaults` values reference existing profile names\n\nOn load: log warnings for invalid fields, apply defaults. On save: reject with errors.\n\n### Step 1.3: Data models\n\n**File:** `vista/server/models/sandbox.py` (new)\n\n```python\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\n\n@dataclass\nclass MountSpec:\n    path: str        # Relative to project root, supports ${FEATURE}\n    mode: str        # \"rw\" or \"ro\"\n\n@dataclass\nclass AccessProfile:\n    name: str\n    mounts: list[MountSpec]\n    network: bool | None = None  # None = inherit global\n\n@dataclass\nclass CredentialDetection:\n    found: bool\n    method: str           # \"env_var\", \"config_dir\", \"config_file\", \"not_found\"\n    source_path: str\n    display_info: str\n\n@dataclass\nclass DockerMount:\n    host_path: str\n    container_path: str\n    mode: str             # \"ro\" or \"rw\"\n\n@dataclass\nclass DockerCredentialConfig:\n    env_vars: dict[str, str] = field(default_factory=dict)\n    mounts: list[DockerMount] = field(default_factory=list)\n\n@dataclass\nclass ContainerInfo:\n    name: str\n    job_id: str\n    provider: str\n    status: str\n    session_id: str\n```\n\n### Step 1.4: Tests\n\n**File:** `vista/tests/test_sandbox_settings.py` (new)\n\n- Defaults application: missing `sandbox` section, partial section, empty section\n- Validation: invalid modes, missing fields, path traversal (`../../../etc`), port out of range\n- Write-back: preserves existing `ralph.defaults`, `ralph.summarizer`, `server.*`\n- `is_sandbox_enabled()` returns correct bool\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2: Credential Management\n\n**Goal:** Implement credential providers that detect host credentials, generate Docker mount/env configs, and support validation.\n\n### Step 2.1: Path translator\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/sandbox/path_translator.py` (new)\n\n```python\nclass PathTranslator:\n    def translate(self, host_path: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Windows: C:\\\\Users\\\\Grove\\\\.ssh → /c/Users/Grove/.ssh\n        Linux/macOS: passthrough\"\"\"\n\n    def get_host_uid_gid(self) -> tuple[int, int]:\n        \"\"\"Windows/WSL2: (1000, 1000). Linux/macOS: os.getuid(), os.getgid()\"\"\"\n```\n\nImplementation:\n- Use `platform.system()` for detection\n- Windows path translation: regex `^([A-Za-z]):\\\\(.*)` → `/$1_lower/$rest_with_forward_slashes`\n- UID/GID: Windows always returns (1000, 1000) since Docker Desktop handles translation. Unix uses `os.getuid()`, `os.getgid()`.\n\n### Step 2.2: Credential providers\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/sandbox/credential_providers.py` (new)\n\nBase class:\n```python\nclass CredentialProvider:\n    name: str\n    display_name: str\n    description: str\n    applies_to: list[str]  # [\"claude\"], [\"*\"], etc.\n\n    def detect(self) -> CredentialDetection: ...\n    def get_docker_config(self) -> DockerCredentialConfig: ...\n    def get_validation_command(self) -> str: ...\n```\n\nBuilt-in providers:\n\n| Provider | `applies_to` | Detects | Mount | Mode |\n|----------|-------------|---------|-------|------|\n| `ClaudeAuthProvider` | `[\"claude\"]` | `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` env, `~/.claude/` dir | `~/.claude/` → `/home/{user}/.claude/` | **rw** |\n| `GitSshProvider` | `[\"*\"]` | `~/.ssh/` with key files | `~/.ssh/` → `/home/{user}/.ssh/` | ro |\n| `GitConfigProvider` | `[\"*\"]` | `~/.gitconfig` file | `~/.gitconfig` → `/home/{user}/.gitconfig` | ro |\n| `GitHubCliProvider` | `[\"*\"]` | `~/.config/gh/` or `%APPDATA%\\GitHub CLI\\` | → `/home/{user}/.config/gh/` | ro |\n| `CustomMountProvider` | `[\"*\"]` | host_path exists | as specified in settings | as specified |\n\nGathering function:\n```python\ndef gather_credentials(provider_name: str, settings: dict) -> list[DockerCredentialConfig]:\n    \"\"\"Filter by applies_to + settings toggles, detect, return configs.\"\"\"\n```\n\nAll providers use `PathTranslator` for host path → Docker path conversion.\n\n### Step 2.3: Tests\n\n**File:** `vista/tests/test_credential_providers.py` (new)\n**File:** `vista/tests/test_path_translator.py` (new)\n\n- Per-provider detection with mocked filesystem (monkeypatch `Path.home()`, `os.environ`)\n- Path translation: `C:\\Users\\Grove\\.ssh` → `/c/Users/Grove/.ssh`\n- Docker config generation: correct mounts and env vars\n- `applies_to` filtering: Claude-only creds skipped for OpenCode loops\n- UID/GID per platform\n- `gather_credentials` end-to-end\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3: Access Profiles\n\n**Goal:** Profile resolution, variable substitution, and Docker mount generation.\n\nCan be developed in parallel with Phase 2 (no interdependency).\n\n### Step 3.1: Profile service\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/sandbox/access_profiles.py` (new)\n\n```python\ndef resolve_profile(\n    explicit: str | None, model: str, settings: dict\n) -> AccessProfile:\n    \"\"\"Priority: explicit override > model_defaults mapping > 'full-access'\"\"\"\n\ndef substitute_variables(mount_path: str, feature: str | None) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Replace ${FEATURE} and ${PROJECT_ROOT} in mount paths.\"\"\"\n\ndef to_docker_mounts(\n    profile: AccessProfile,\n    project_root: Path,\n    feature: str | None,\n    translator: PathTranslator,\n) -> list[dict]:\n    \"\"\"Convert profile mounts to Docker bind mount specs.\n    Special case: path '.' → mount entire project root as /workspace/\n    Skip non-existent paths with warning (not error).\n    \"\"\"\n\ndef validate_profile(profile_dict: dict) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"Validate: ≥1 mount, paths relative, no '..', valid modes.\"\"\"\n\ndef check_network_compatibility(\n    profile: AccessProfile, provider_name: str, global_network: bool\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Raise ValueError if OpenCode + network disabled.\"\"\"\n```\n\nNetwork policy resolution: `profile.network if profile.network is not None else global_network`\n\n### Step 3.2: Tests\n\n**File:** `vista/tests/test_access_profiles.py` (new)\n\n- Resolution chain: explicit > model_defaults > fallback\n- Variable substitution: `${FEATURE}` → slug, `${PROJECT_ROOT}` → `/workspace`\n- Mount translation: `\".\"` → full project root, relative paths → `/workspace/{path}`\n- Validation: reject `..`, reject absolute paths, require ≥1 mount\n- Network: OpenCode + `network: false` → error with clear message\n- Missing path: skipped with warning\n\n---\n\n## Phase 4: Container Lifecycle Management\n\n**Goal:** Docker container creation, execution, monitoring, teardown, and image management.\n\n### Step 4.1: ContainerManager\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/sandbox/container_manager.py` (new)\n\n**New dependency:** `docker` Python SDK (`pip install docker`). Import lazily to avoid breaking the plugin when Docker SDK is not installed.\n\n```python\nclass ContainerManager:\n    def __init__(self, session_id: str):\n        import docker\n        self.docker = docker.from_env()\n        self.session_id = session_id\n\n    async def create_loop_container(\n        self,\n        job_id: str,\n        provider_name: str,\n        project_root: Path,\n        profile_mounts: list[dict],\n        credentials: list[DockerCredentialConfig],\n        image: str,\n        network: bool = True,\n        env_extra: dict | None = None,\n    ) -> ContainerInfo:\n        \"\"\"\n        1. Combine profile_mounts + credential mounts\n        2. Combine credential env_vars + env_extra + DEVCONTAINER=true\n        3. docker.containers.create() with labels, user, extra_hosts\n        4. container.start()\n        \"\"\"\n\n    async def exec_in_container(\n        self,\n        container_name: str,\n        command: list[str],\n        workdir: str = \"/workspace\",\n        env: dict | None = None,\n        stdout_handle=None,\n    ) -> int:  # returns host PID\n        \"\"\"docker exec — run command inside running container.\"\"\"\n\n    async def remove_container(self, container_name: str) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Stop (timeout=10) + remove container.\"\"\"\n\n    async def cleanup_orphans(self) -> list[str]:\n        \"\"\"Find containers with managed-by=vista-ralph where\n        vista-session != self.session_id. Stop + remove. Return names.\"\"\"\n\n    async def shutdown_all(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Stop + remove all containers with managed-by=vista-ralph\n        AND vista-session == self.session_id.\"\"\"\n\n    def list_containers(self) -> list[ContainerInfo]:\n        \"\"\"List all managed containers with status.\"\"\"\n\n    def is_docker_available(self) -> tuple[bool, str]:\n        \"\"\"Try docker.ping(). Return (True, \"Docker running\") or (False, reason).\"\"\"\n\n    async def ensure_image(self, image_name: str = \"vista-ralph:latest\") -> str:\n        \"\"\"Check if image exists locally. If not, build from bundled Dockerfile.\n        Store Dockerfile hash to detect changes.\"\"\"\n```\n\nContainer creation details (from container-lifecycle spec):\n- Name: `vista-ralph-{job_id[:8]}`\n- Labels: `managed-by=vista-ralph`, `vista-job-id={job_id}`, `vista-provider={provider}`, `vista-session={session_id}`, `vista-project={hash(project_root)[:8]}`\n- Command: `sleep infinity` (keeps container alive for exec)\n- `extra_hosts={\"host.docker.internal\": \"host-gateway\"}` (Linux compatibility)\n- `user=f\"{uid}:{gid}\"`\n- `working_dir=\"/workspace\"`\n- `network_mode=\"bridge\" if network else \"none\"`\n\n### Step 4.2: Docker image\n\n**File:** `vista/docker/Dockerfile` (new)\n\nBased on claudebox reference (`reference/claudebox/build/Dockerfile`) with simplifications:\n\n- Base: `debian:bookworm`\n- Build args: `USER_ID`, `GROUP_ID`, `NODE_VERSION`\n- Install: git, node (via nvm), claude-code CLI, python3, uv, gh CLI, jq, curl, bash\n- User creation with UID/GID matching\n- `DEVCONTAINER=true`\n- `WORKDIR /workspace`\n- Remove: zsh/fzf customization, tmux config, delta, firewall scripts, entrypoint scripts\n- Simple entrypoint: just `sleep infinity` (Vista uses `docker exec`)\n\n**File:** `vista/docker/.dockerignore` (new)\n\n### Step 4.3: Tests\n\n**File:** `vista/tests/test_container_manager.py` (new)\n\n- Container naming and label generation (unit, no Docker)\n- Volume mount construction from profile + credentials (unit)\n- Docker availability check (mock docker client)\n- Create → exec → remove flow (mock docker client)\n- Orphan cleanup: mock containers from \"old session\" are removed, current session containers preserved\n\n---\n\n## Phase 5: OpenCode Serve Management & Proxy\n\n**Goal:** Host-side `opencode serve` process management and Vista proxy endpoint.\n\n### Step 5.1: OpenCodeServeManager\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/sandbox/opencode_serve_manager.py` (new)\n\n```python\nclass OpenCodeServeManager:\n    def __init__(self, port: int = 4096):\n        self.port = port\n        self.process: subprocess.Popen | None = None\n        self.sessions: dict[str, str] = {}  # job_id → session_id\n\n    async def ensure_running(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Start 'opencode serve --port {port} --hostname 127.0.0.1'\n        if not running. Health check: GET http://localhost:{port}/doc\"\"\"\n\n    async def create_session(self, job_id: str, cwd: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"POST to opencode serve to create session. Return session_id.\"\"\"\n\n    async def close_session(self, job_id: str) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Close session. Remove from self.sessions.\"\"\"\n\n    async def stop(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Terminate opencode serve process.\"\"\"\n\n    def is_running(self) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Process alive + health check passes.\"\"\"\n```\n\n### Step 5.2: Sandbox API routes\n\n**File:** `vista/server/routes/sandbox.py` (new)\n\n```python\nrouter = APIRouter(prefix=\"/api/sandbox\", tags=[\"sandbox\"])\n\n@router.post(\"/opencode/{session_id}/message\")\nasync def opencode_proxy_message(session_id: str, request: Request):\n    \"\"\"Forward message from container to opencode serve on host.\n    1. Validate session_id exists\n    2. Forward request body to http://localhost:{port}/...\n    3. Stream response back to caller\n    \"\"\"\n\n@router.get(\"/status\")\nasync def sandbox_status():\n    \"\"\"Returns { docker_available, docker_running, image_built, image_name }\"\"\"\n\n@router.put(\"/settings\")\nasync def update_sandbox_settings(body: dict):\n    \"\"\"Toggle sandbox.enabled. Writes to settings.json.\"\"\"\n\n@router.post(\"/credentials/validate\")\nasync def validate_credentials():\n    \"\"\"Spin up temp container, run validation commands, tear down.\"\"\"\n\n@router.post(\"/image/build\")\nasync def build_image():\n    \"\"\"Trigger sandbox image rebuild.\"\"\"\n```\n\n### Step 5.3: Tests\n\n**File:** `vista/tests/test_opencode_serve_manager.py` (new)\n\n- `ensure_running` with mock subprocess\n- Session create/close with mock HTTP\n- Health check logic\n- Process lifecycle\n\n**File:** `vista/tests/test_sandbox_api.py` (new)\n\n- `GET /api/sandbox/status` returns correct Docker/image state\n- `PUT /api/sandbox/settings` with enabled true/false\n- Proxy endpoint forwards correctly (mock opencode serve)\n\n---\n\n## Phase 6: RalphService Integration\n\n**Goal:** Add sandbox branch to `RalphService` so `create_job()` routes through Docker when enabled. This is the core integration point.\n\n### Step 6.1: Sandbox branch in `create_job()`\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/ralph_service.py` (modify)\n\nAdd at the top of `create_job()`:\n\n```python\nsandbox_settings = config.get_sandbox_settings()\nif sandbox_settings.get(\"enabled\"):\n    return self._create_sandbox_job(\n        job_dir, project_root, slug, mode, task_description,\n        provider, model, iterations, sandbox_settings, job_id\n    )\n# else: existing local subprocess code stays unchanged\n```\n\n**New method `_create_sandbox_job()` (Claude Code path):**\n\n1. Generate `loop.sh` (always bash — container is Linux)\n   - Use existing `LOOP_SCRIPT_TEMPLATE` content but get invocation via `provider.get_invocation(\"sh\")`\n   - The Claude invocation block already supports bash: `printf \"%s\" \"$PROMPT_CONTENT\" | claude -p ...`\n2. Resolve access profile: `resolve_profile(explicit=None, model=model, settings=sandbox_settings)`\n3. Convert profile to Docker mounts: `to_docker_mounts(profile, project_root, slug, translator)`\n4. Gather credentials: `gather_credentials(\"claude\", sandbox_settings)`\n5. Check network compatibility\n6. `container_manager.create_loop_container(job_id, \"claude\", project_root, profile_mounts, credentials, image, network)`\n7. `pid = container_manager.exec_in_container(container_name, [\"bash\", f\"/workspace/.vista/ralph/{slug}-{job_id[:8]}/loop.sh\"], stdout_handle=output_log)`\n8. Save job.json with: `sandbox: True, container: \"vista-ralph-{job_id[:8]}\", pid: exec_pid`\n\n**New method `_create_sandbox_job()` (OpenCode path):**\n\nSame as Claude but additionally:\n1. `opencode_serve_manager.ensure_running()`\n2. `session_id = opencode_serve_manager.create_session(job_id, str(project_root))`\n3. Generate `loop.sh` from **new** `OPENCODE_SANDBOX_LOOP_TEMPLATE`\n4. Gather credentials: `gather_credentials(\"opencode\", sandbox_settings)` — no AI creds\n5. Exec with extra env: `VISTA_HOST=host.docker.internal, VISTA_PORT={port}, OPENCODE_SESSION={session_id}, MODEL={model}`\n6. Save job.json with additional `opencode_session` field\n\n### Step 6.2: OpenCode sandbox loop template\n\n**File:** `vista/portable/ralph.py` (modify — add constant)\n\nAdd `OPENCODE_SANDBOX_LOOP_TEMPLATE` — a bash script that:\n- Reads PROMPT + task.md + progress.txt (same compose logic as current template)\n- Uses `curl -s -X POST \"$VISTA_API/message\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d ...` to call Vista proxy\n- Pushes via git after each iteration\n- Checks completion markers (`ALL PHASES COMPLETE`, `Reached max iterations`)\n- Variables: `VISTA_HOST`, `VISTA_PORT`, `OPENCODE_SESSION`, `MODEL` from env\n\nFull template content is in the ralph-mcp-integration spec (lines 95-185).\n\n### Step 6.3: Modify `stop_job()`\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/ralph_service.py` (modify)\n\n```python\ndef stop_job(self, project_root, job_id):\n    # ... load job ...\n    if job.get(\"sandbox\"):\n        self._kill_pid(job[\"pid\"])  # Kill exec process\n        if job.get(\"opencode_session\"):\n            await opencode_serve_manager.close_session(job_id)\n        await container_manager.remove_container(f\"vista-ralph-{job_id[:8]}\")\n    else:\n        # Current behavior unchanged\n```\n\n### Step 6.4: Modify `get_job_status()`\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/ralph_service.py` (modify)\n\nWhen `job.get(\"sandbox\")` and PID is not running:\n- Also check if container still exists (container_manager.list_containers)\n- If container gone + PID gone: apply existing completion detection logic\n\n### Step 6.5: Job metadata extension\n\nWhen sandbox active, `job.json` includes:\n```json\n{\n  \"sandbox\": true,\n  \"container\": \"vista-ralph-{job_id[:8]}\",\n  \"opencode_session\": \"sess_xyz\"  // OpenCode only\n}\n```\n\nWhen sandbox disabled: `sandbox` key absent (backward compatible).\n\n### Step 6.6: Tests\n\n**File:** `vista/tests/test_ralph_service.py` (modify — add test cases)\n\n- `create_job()` routes to ContainerManager when `sandbox.enabled = true`\n- `create_job()` uses local subprocess when `sandbox.enabled = false`\n- Claude loops generate bash `loop.sh` with native `claude -p`\n- OpenCode loops generate bash `loop.sh` with `curl` calls\n- `job.json` includes `sandbox`, `container`, `opencode_session` when active\n- `stop_job()` kills PID + removes container + closes session\n\n---\n\n## Phase 7: App Lifecycle Integration\n\n**Goal:** Wire sandbox managers into Vista's startup/shutdown and register routes.\n\n### Step 7.1: Sandbox initialization module\n\n**File:** `vista/server/services/sandbox/__init__.py` (modify to add global accessors)\n\n```python\n_container_manager: ContainerManager | None = None\n_opencode_serve_manager: OpenCodeServeManager | None = None\n\nasync def init_sandbox() -> None:\n    \"\"\"Called during app startup. Initializes managers if sandbox enabled.\"\"\"\n    global _container_manager, _opencode_serve_manager\n    if not config.is_sandbox_enabled():\n        return\n    session_id = str(uuid4())\n    try:\n        _container_manager = ContainerManager(session_id)\n        orphans = await _container_manager.cleanup_orphans()\n        if orphans:\n            logger.info(f\"Cleaned up {len(orphans)} orphaned containers: {orphans}\")\n        await _container_manager.ensure_image()\n    except Exception as e:\n        logger.error(f\"Sandbox init failed: {e}. Sandbox will be unavailable.\")\n        _container_manager = None\n    serve_settings = config.get_opencode_serve_settings()\n    _opencode_serve_manager = OpenCodeServeManager(serve_settings[\"port\"])\n\nasync def shutdown_sandbox() -> None:\n    \"\"\"Called during app shutdown.\"\"\"\n    if _container_manager:\n        await _container_manager.shutdown_all()\n    if _opencode_serve_manager:\n        await _opencode_serve_manager.stop()\n\ndef get_container_manager() -> ContainerManager | None:\n    return _container_manager\n\ndef get_opencode_serve_manager() -> OpenCodeServeManager | None:\n    return _opencode_serve_manager\n```\n\n### Step 7.2: Modify app lifespan\n\n**File:** `vista/server/app.py` (modify)\n\n```python\n@asynccontextmanager\nasync def lifespan(app: FastAPI):\n    config.ensure_full_path()\n    config.DATA_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    (config.DATA_DIR / \"sessions\").mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n    # NEW: sandbox initialization\n    from server.services.sandbox import init_sandbox, shutdown_sandbox\n    await init_sandbox()\n    yield\n    await loop_service.stop_all()\n    await diagram_watcher.stop()\n    keepalive_manager.stop_all()\n    # NEW: sandbox shutdown\n    await shutdown_sandbox()\n```\n\nRegister sandbox routes:\n```python\nfrom server.routes import sandbox\napp.include_router(sandbox.router)\n```\n\n### Step 7.3: Credential validation at startup\n\nInside `init_sandbox()`, after image is ensured:\n- Run `validate_credentials()` — creates temp container, runs validation commands per enabled provider\n- Log results (pass/fail per credential) to server output\n- Non-blocking: validation failures are warnings, not startup failures\n\n---\n\n## Phase 8: Dashboard UI\n\n**Goal:** Single toggle + inline Docker status in Ralph settings page.\n\n### Step 8.1: Frontend\n\n**File:** `vista/server/views/ralph_settings.html` (modify)\n\nAdd \"Docker Sandbox\" section after existing ralph settings controls:\n\n```\nDocker Sandbox  [toggle: OFF/ON]   {inline status text}\n```\n\nBehavior:\n- Toggle reads/writes `sandbox.enabled` via `PUT /api/sandbox/settings`\n- When toggled ON: call `GET /api/sandbox/status`, display status:\n  - Green dot + \"Docker running\" (available + image built)\n  - Amber dot + \"Building image...\" (available + image building)\n  - Red dot + \"Docker not running\" (installed but stopped)\n  - Red dot + \"Docker Desktop required\" (not installed)\n- When toggled OFF: hide status text\n- Status checked on page load (if ON) and on toggle change\n- No polling — manual refresh\n\n### Step 8.2: Tests\n\n**File:** `vista/tests/test_sandbox_api.py` (extend from Phase 5.3)\n\n- `GET /api/sandbox/status` returns correct states\n- `PUT /api/sandbox/settings` toggles correctly\n- Error states display actionable guidance\n\n---\n\n## Phase 9: Integration Testing\n\n**File:** `vista/tests/integration/test_sandbox_lifecycle.py` (new)\n\nRequires Docker to be installed and running:\n\n- Full `ralph_start → ralph_status → ralph_stop` with sandbox (Claude path)\n- Full cycle with sandbox (OpenCode path via serve proxy)\n- `ralph_summary` reads artifacts produced inside container\n- Orphan cleanup across Vista restarts\n- Concurrent loops in separate containers\n- Bypass mode: `sandbox.enabled = false` runs identically to pre-sandbox\n- Agent can access `.vista/features/`, source code, `.git/` from inside container\n- Agent can `git push` from inside container (SSH keys mounted)\n\n---\n\n## File Summary\n\n### New Files (17)\n\n| File | Phase | Purpose |\n|------|-------|---------|\n| `vista/server/models/sandbox.py` | 1 | Data models (MountSpec, AccessProfile, DockerMount, etc.) |\n| `vista/server/services/sandbox_settings.py` | 1 | Settings validation |\n| `vista/server/services/sandbox/__init__.py` | 2+ | Package init + global accessors + init/shutdown |\n| `vista/server/services/sandbox/path_translator.py` | 2 | Host→Docker path conversion + UID/GID |\n| `vista/server/services/sandbox/credential_providers.py` | 2 | 5 credential providers + gathering |\n| `vista/server/services/sandbox/access_profiles.py` | 3 | Profile resolution, variable substitution, mount translation |\n| `vista/server/services/sandbox/container_manager.py` | 4 | Container lifecycle (create, exec, remove, cleanup, image) |\n| `vista/server/services/sandbox/opencode_serve_manager.py` | 5 | Host-side `opencode serve` management |\n| `vista/server/routes/sandbox.py` | 5 | API endpoints (status, settings, proxy, validate, build) |\n| `vista/docker/Dockerfile` | 4 | Modified claudebox image for Vista sandbox |\n| `vista/docker/.dockerignore` | 4 | Build context ignore |\n| `vista/tests/test_sandbox_settings.py` | 1 | Settings tests |\n| `vista/tests/test_path_translator.py` | 2 | Path translation tests |\n| `vista/tests/test_credential_providers.py` | 2 | Credential provider tests |\n| `vista/tests/test_access_profiles.py` | 3 | Access profile tests |\n| `vista/tests/test_container_manager.py` | 4 | Container lifecycle tests |\n| `vista/tests/test_opencode_serve_manager.py` | 5 | OpenCode serve tests |\n\n### Modified Files (5)\n\n| File | Phase | Changes |\n|------|-------|---------|\n| `vista/server/config.py` | 1 | Add `_SANDBOX_DEFAULTS` + getter/setter functions |\n| `vista/server/services/ralph_service.py` | 6 | Sandbox branch in `create_job()`, `stop_job()`, `get_job_status()` |\n| `vista/portable/ralph.py` | 6 | Add `OPENCODE_SANDBOX_LOOP_TEMPLATE` |\n| `vista/server/app.py` | 7 | Lifespan: init/shutdown sandbox. Register sandbox routes. |\n| `vista/server/views/ralph_settings.html` | 8 | Sandbox toggle + inline Docker status |\n\n### New Dependencies\n\n| Package | Purpose | Install |\n|---------|---------|---------|\n| `docker` | Python Docker SDK for container management | `pip install docker` |\n\nImport lazily — if not installed, sandbox features disabled with clear error. Plugin still functions for non-sandbox usage.\n\n---\n\n## Build Order\n\n```\nPhase 1 (Settings + Models)         ← Foundation\n  ↓\nPhase 2 (Credentials) ─────┐\nPhase 3 (Access Profiles) ──┤       ← Parallel (no interdependency)\n  ↓                         ↓\nPhase 4 (ContainerManager)          ← Core infrastructure\n  ↓\nPhase 5 (OpenCode Serve + API)      ← Second execution path\n  ↓\nPhase 6 (RalphService Integration)  ← Ties everything together\n  ↓\nPhase 7 (App Lifecycle)             ← Startup/shutdown wiring\n  ↓\nPhase 8 (Dashboard UI) ────┐\nPhase 9 (Integration Tests) ┤      ← Parallel (independent)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Spec Alignment Matrix\n\n| Domain Requirement | Implementing Spec | Phase |\n|---|---|---|\n| Prevent file access outside project | access-profiles (container isolation) | 3, 4 |\n| Eliminate credential complexity for OpenCode | credential-management (host-side serve) | 2, 5 |\n| Claudebox as base image | container-lifecycle | 4 |\n| Transparent sandbox (no MCP changes) | ralph-mcp-integration | 6 |\n| Agent access to feature specs | access-profiles (\"full-access\" default) | 3 |\n| Full bypass when disabled | settings, ralph-mcp-integration | 1, 6 |\n| Container-per-loop isolation | container-lifecycle | 4 |\n| Orphan cleanup on startup | container-lifecycle | 7 |\n| Single dashboard toggle | dashboard-ui | 8 |\n| Zero Docker knowledge required | dashboard-ui, settings | 1, 8 |\n| Credential auto-detection | credential-management | 2 |\n| Credential validation at startup | credential-management | 7 |\n| OpenCode serve management | container-lifecycle | 5 |\n| Vista proxy for OpenCode | ralph-mcp-integration | 5 |\n| Path translation (Windows→Docker) | credential-management | 2 |\n| UID/GID matching | credential-management | 2 |\n| Docker availability check | dashboard-ui, container-lifecycle | 4, 8 |\n| Settings validation | settings | 1 |\n| No changes to MCP tool interface | ralph-mcp-integration | 6 (transparent) |\n\n---\n\n## Risk Mitigation\n\n| Risk | Mitigation |\n|---|---|\n| Docker not installed | Lazy import of `docker` SDK. Sandbox marked unavailable. Loops run locally. |\n| Docker not running | `is_docker_available()` check. Dashboard shows actionable guidance. |\n| WSL2 bind mount performance | Acceptable per NFR. Document in known limitations. |\n| Port conflict for opencode serve | Log error, try next available port. |\n| Concurrent loops git conflicts | Documented: separate containers, shared files. Users should use separate branches. |\n| Orphaned containers after crash | Session-based cleanup on every Vista startup. |\n| UID/GID mismatch | Host UID/GID as build args. Windows defaults to 1000:1000. |\n| `~/.claude/` must be rw | Explicitly mounted read-write (differs from claudebox copy pattern). |\n| SSH agent forwarding | Not supported in v1. Only file-based SSH keys. Documented. |\n","numLines":820,"startLine":1,"totalLines":820}}}
