{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013ijrwuHHcRKx8iPCfeVfWv","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Spec: Settings and Image\n     2→\n     3→## Overview\n     4→Defines sandbox configuration in settings.json and manages Docker image auto-build from the claudebox base image for Vista-sandboxed execution.\n     5→\n     6→## Changelog\n     7→| Date | ID | Change | Reason | Commit |\n     8→|------|-----|--------|--------|--------|\n     9→| 2026-02-12 | --- | Created | Initial spec generation | --- |\n    10→\n    11→## Parent JTBD\n    12→Provide configurable sandbox settings and a ready-to-use Docker image so that sandboxed jobs can launch quickly with minimal user setup.\n    13→\n    14→## Scope\n    15→**In Scope:**\n    16→- SANDBOX_CONFIG section within settings.json schema\n    17→- Configuration fields: image name, network mode, TTL, credential mount enable/disable\n    18→- Docker image management: check existence, auto-build on first use, rebuild on demand\n    19→- Claudebox base image integration and extension with Vista tooling\n    20→- Image caching for fast subsequent job launches\n    21→- Docker SDK connection validation (Layer 1 testing)\n    22→- `GET /api/ralph/sandbox/status` response data (Docker installed, daemon running, image exists)\n    23→- `POST /api/ralph/sandbox/build` handler logic\n    24→\n    25→**Out of Scope:**\n    26→- Container creation and lifecycle (see container-lifecycle spec)\n    27→- Credential mount path resolution (see credential-management spec)\n    28→- Loop script generation (see bash-loop-generation spec)\n    29→- RalphService integration logic (see ralph-sandbox-integration spec)\n    30→- Docker Desktop installation or licensing\n    31→- Custom Dockerfile authoring by users\n    32→- Multi-image support (single image in v1)\n    33→\n    34→## Requirements\n    35→### Functional\n    36→1. **DS-F45:** settings.json SHALL support a `sandbox` section under the `ralph` configuration key with the following fields: `image` (str, default \"vista-ralph:latest\"), `network_enabled` (bool, default true), `ttl_seconds` (int, default 7200), `credential_mounts` (object).\n    37→2. **DS-F46:** The `credential_mounts` config object SHALL contain entries for each credential type (`claude_auth`, `git_ssh`, `git_config`, `gh_cli`, `opencode`) each with an `enabled` (bool, default true) field.\n    38→3. **DS-F47:** ContainerManager SHALL expose an `ensure_image(check_only=False)` method that checks if the configured image exists locally and, when `check_only=False` and image is missing, triggers an automatic build.\n    39→4. **DS-F48:** The Docker image SHALL be built from the RchGrav/claudebox base image, extended with any Vista-specific tooling (e.g., git, curl) if not already present in claudebox.\n    40→5. **DS-F49:** Image build progress SHALL be reported via a callback mechanism so callers (MCP tools, API) can surface \"Building Docker image...\" status to the user.\n    41→6. **DS-F50:** The `POST /api/ralph/sandbox/build` endpoint SHALL force a rebuild of the Docker image even if one already exists, replacing the previous image.\n    42→7. **DS-F51:** The `GET /api/ralph/sandbox/status` endpoint SHALL return a JSON object with `docker_installed` (bool), `daemon_running` (bool), `image_exists` (bool), and `image_name` (str).\n    43→8. **DS-F52:** When the Docker Python SDK (`docker` package) is not installed, `docker_installed` SHALL be False and all sandbox operations SHALL raise a clear error: \"Docker SDK not installed. Run: pip install docker\".\n    44→9. **DS-F53:** When the Docker daemon is not running, `daemon_running` SHALL be False and sandbox operations SHALL raise: \"Docker daemon is not running. Please start Docker Desktop.\"\n    45→10. **DS-F54:** The image build SHALL use a Dockerfile stored within the Vista plugin directory (e.g., `vista/docker/Dockerfile`) that extends claudebox.\n    46→11. **DS-F55:** Settings SHALL be validated on load: invalid `ttl_seconds` (negative or zero) SHALL be rejected, invalid image names SHALL be rejected.\n    47→\n    48→### Non-Functional\n    49→1. **DS-NF10:** Image build time SHALL be under 5 minutes on a standard internet connection (first build, uncached).\n    50→2. **DS-NF11:** Image existence check SHALL complete in under 1 second.\n    51→3. **DS-NF12:** Settings defaults SHALL allow sandbox to work with zero configuration beyond having Docker installed.\n    52→\n    53→## User Workflows\n    54→### Workflow: First Sandboxed Job (Image Auto-Build)\n    55→**Actor:** User via Claude/MCP\n    56→**Trigger:** First `ralph_start` with `sandbox=true` when no image exists\n    57→**Steps:**\n    58→1. RalphService calls ContainerManager.ensure_image()\n    59→2. ContainerManager checks for image via Docker SDK: `client.images.get(\"vista-ralph:latest\")`\n    60→3. Image not found: ContainerManager triggers build from Dockerfile\n    61→4. Build progress reported to caller: \"Building Docker image (first time setup, ~2-5 minutes)...\"\n    62→5. Build completes, image tagged as \"vista-ralph:latest\"\n    63→6. ContainerManager returns success, job creation continues\n    64→**Error Cases:**\n    65→- Dockerfile not found: \"Vista Dockerfile not found at {path}. Plugin may be corrupted.\"\n    66→- Build fails (network error): \"Image build failed: {build_log_tail}. Check network and retry with POST /api/ralph/sandbox/build\"\n    67→- Build fails (Dockerfile error): \"Image build failed: {build_log_tail}. Please report this issue.\"\n    68→- Claudebox base image not pullable: \"Cannot pull claudebox base image. Check Docker network access.\"\n    69→\n    70→### Workflow: Manual Image Rebuild\n    71→**Actor:** User via dashboard or API\n    72→**Trigger:** `POST /api/ralph/sandbox/build`\n    73→**Steps:**\n    74→1. API handler calls ContainerManager.ensure_image(force_rebuild=True)\n    75→2. ContainerManager removes existing image (if any)\n    76→3. ContainerManager builds fresh image from Dockerfile\n    77→4. Returns build result with image ID and size\n    78→**Error Cases:**\n    79→- Image in use by running container: \"Cannot rebuild image while sandboxed jobs are running. Stop all sandboxed jobs first.\"\n    80→\n    81→### Workflow: Check Sandbox Readiness\n    82→**Actor:** User or dashboard\n    83→**Trigger:** `GET /api/ralph/sandbox/status`\n    84→**Steps:**\n    85→1. API handler attempts lazy import of `docker` package\n    86→2. If import fails: return `{docker_installed: false, daemon_running: false, image_exists: false, image_name: \"vista-ralph:latest\"}`\n    87→3. If import succeeds: attempt `docker.from_env().ping()`\n    88→4. If ping fails: return `{docker_installed: true, daemon_running: false, image_exists: false, image_name: \"vista-ralph:latest\"}`\n    89→5. If ping succeeds: check `client.images.get(image_name)`\n    90→6. Return full status: `{docker_installed: true, daemon_running: true, image_exists: bool, image_name: \"vista-ralph:latest\"}`\n    91→**Error Cases:**\n    92→- Unexpected Docker API error: return `{docker_installed: true, daemon_running: false, ...}` with error detail\n    93→\n    94→### Workflow: User Customizes Sandbox Settings\n    95→**Actor:** User editing settings.json\n    96→**Trigger:** User wants to change TTL or disable network\n    97→**Steps:**\n    98→1. User opens settings.json, adds/modifies `ralph.sandbox` section\n    99→2. Sets `network_enabled: false` for offline sandbox\n   100→3. Sets `ttl_seconds: 3600` for shorter TTL\n   101→4. Next sandboxed job uses updated settings\n   102→**Error Cases:**\n   103→- Invalid TTL (negative): validation rejects on settings load, uses default\n   104→\n   105→## Data Model\n   106→**Entities:**\n   107→- `SANDBOX_CONFIG`: `image` (str), `network_enabled` (bool), `ttl_seconds` (int), `credential_mounts` (dict of CredentialMountConfig)\n   108→- `CredentialMountConfig`: `enabled` (bool)\n   109→\n   110→**Relationships:**\n   111→- SETTINGS contains zero or one SANDBOX_CONFIG\n   112→- SANDBOX_CONFIG contains zero or more CredentialMountConfig entries\n   113→\n   114→### Settings Schema Example\n   115→```json\n   116→{\n   117→  \"ralph\": {\n   118→    \"sandbox\": {\n   119→      \"image\": \"vista-ralph:latest\",\n   120→      \"network_enabled\": true,\n   121→      \"ttl_seconds\": 7200,\n   122→      \"credential_mounts\": {\n   123→        \"claude_auth\": { \"enabled\": true },\n   124→        \"git_ssh\": { \"enabled\": true },\n   125→        \"git_config\": { \"enabled\": true },\n   126→        \"gh_cli\": { \"enabled\": true },\n   127→        \"opencode\": { \"enabled\": true }\n   128→      }\n   129→    }\n   130→  }\n   131→}\n   132→```\n   133→\n   134→## Integration Points\n   135→**Dependencies:**\n   136→- Docker Python SDK (`docker` package, lazily imported)\n   137→- Docker daemon (for image operations)\n   138→- RchGrav/claudebox Docker image (base image pulled during build)\n   139→- Vista plugin directory (for Dockerfile location)\n   140→- settings.json loader (existing config infrastructure)\n   141→\n   142→**Provides to:**\n   143→- ContainerManager: image name and sandbox configuration\n   144→- CredentialMounter: credential_mounts enable/disable flags\n   145→- ContainerManager: TTL and network settings\n   146→- RalphService: sandbox config for job creation decisions\n   147→- API routes: sandbox status and build endpoints\n   148→\n   149→## Technical Considerations\n   150→### Architecture\n   151→- SANDBOX_CONFIG parsed by existing settings loader with defaults for all fields\n   152→- Dockerfile stored at `vista/docker/Dockerfile` (or `vista/docker/Dockerfile.sandbox`)\n   153→- Image management methods on ContainerManager (or separate ImageManager if complexity warrants)\n   154→- Docker client created lazily and cached for session lifetime\n   155→\n   156→### Patterns\n   157→- Configuration with defaults: every field has a sensible default, sandbox works with zero config\n   158→- Lazy loading: Docker SDK import deferred until first sandbox operation\n   159→- Builder pattern potential: Dockerfile could be generated programmatically if claudebox extensions vary\n   160→\n   161→### Libraries/APIs\n   162→- `docker.from_env()`: create Docker client from environment\n   163→- `client.images.get(name)`: check image existence\n   164→- `client.images.build(path, tag)`: build image from Dockerfile\n   165→- `client.images.remove(name)`: remove image for rebuild\n   166→- `client.ping()`: verify daemon connectivity\n   167→\n   168→### Dockerfile Structure (conceptual)\n   169→```dockerfile\n   170→FROM ghcr.io/rchgrav/claudebox:latest\n   171→\n   172→# Vista-specific additions (if needed)\n   173→RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y git curl && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*\n   174→\n   175→# Create non-root user matching host UID/GID (set at build or runtime)\n   176→ARG UID=1000\n   177→ARG GID=1000\n   178→RUN groupadd -g $GID user && useradd -m -u $UID -g $GID user\n   179→\n   180→USER user\n   181→WORKDIR /workspace\n   182→```\n   183→\n   184→## Related Diagrams\n   185→- `arch/data-model.mmd` -- SETTINGS, SANDBOX_CONFIG, and CREDENTIAL_MOUNT entities\n   186→- `arch/state-container.mmd` -- ImageCheck and Building states in container lifecycle\n   187→- `arch/user-flow.mmd` -- Docker image check and auto-build decision flow\n   188→- `arch/sequence-sandboxed-job.mmd` -- ensure_image() call in job creation sequence\n   189→\n   190→## Acceptance Criteria\n   191→- [ ] DS-F45: settings.json supports `ralph.sandbox` with image, network_enabled, ttl_seconds, credential_mounts\n   192→- [ ] DS-F45: Default values applied when sandbox section is absent: image=\"vista-ralph:latest\", network_enabled=true, ttl_seconds=7200\n   193→- [ ] DS-F46: Each credential type has an `enabled` field defaulting to true\n   194→- [ ] DS-F47: `ensure_image()` returns True when image exists without triggering build\n   195→- [ ] DS-F47: `ensure_image()` triggers build when image missing and check_only=False\n   196→- [ ] DS-F47: `ensure_image(check_only=True)` returns False when image missing, does not build\n   197→- [ ] DS-F48: Built image is based on claudebox and tagged as configured image name\n   198→- [ ] DS-F49: Build progress callback invoked during image build\n   199→- [ ] DS-F50: `POST /api/ralph/sandbox/build` rebuilds image even when one exists\n   200→- [ ] DS-F51: `GET /api/ralph/sandbox/status` returns correct JSON with all four fields\n   201→- [ ] DS-F52: Docker SDK not installed produces clear error message with install instruction\n   202→- [ ] DS-F53: Docker daemon not running produces clear error message mentioning Docker Desktop\n   203→- [ ] DS-F54: Dockerfile exists at expected path within Vista plugin directory\n   204→- [ ] DS-F55: Negative ttl_seconds rejected on settings validation\n   205→- [ ] DS-NF10: Image build completes within 5 minutes on standard connection\n   206→- [ ] DS-NF11: Image existence check completes under 1 second\n   207→- [ ] DS-NF12: Sandbox works with only Docker installed and zero settings changes\n   208→\n   209→## Testing Strategy\n   210→> Docker SDK connection testing (Layer 1) maps to this spec. Image management is part of ContainerManager TDD.\n   211→\n   212→**TDD Required:** Partial (settings validation is testable without Docker; Docker connection is integration)\n   213→\n   214→### Test Cases (from domain requirements Layer 1)\n   215→#### Happy Path\n   216→- `test_docker_sdk_import_succeeds`: `import docker` succeeds when package installed\n   217→- `test_docker_daemon_ping_succeeds`: `docker.from_env().ping()` returns True (integration, requires Docker)\n   218→- `test_image_exists_check`: `client.images.get(\"vista-ralph:latest\")` returns image object (integration)\n   219→- `test_settings_defaults_applied`: Missing sandbox section produces correct defaults\n   220→- `test_settings_custom_values`: Custom ttl_seconds and network_enabled parsed correctly\n   221→- `test_credential_mounts_config_parsed`: All five credential types with enabled flags parsed\n   222→- `test_sandbox_status_all_available`: Returns all true when Docker and image ready\n   223→- `test_sandbox_status_no_docker`: Returns docker_installed=false\n   224→\n   225→#### Edge Cases\n   226→- `test_settings_partial_sandbox_config`: Only image specified, rest default\n   227→- `test_settings_partial_credential_mounts`: Only some credential types configured, rest default to enabled\n   228→- `test_ensure_image_concurrent_calls`: Two simultaneous ensure_image calls do not duplicate builds\n   229→- `test_rebuild_when_no_existing_image`: force_rebuild with no existing image just builds fresh\n   230→\n   231→#### Error Conditions\n   232→- `test_docker_sdk_not_installed`: Import fails gracefully with clear error message\n   233→- `test_docker_daemon_not_running`: Ping fails with clear error message\n   234→- `test_image_build_network_failure`: Build fails with network error, returns useful message\n   235→- `test_invalid_ttl_negative`: Negative ttl_seconds rejected at settings load\n   236→- `test_invalid_ttl_zero`: Zero ttl_seconds rejected at settings load\n   237→- `test_dockerfile_not_found`: Missing Dockerfile raises clear error with path\n   238→\n   239→### Test Data Requirements\n   240→- Test settings.json with various sandbox configurations (full, partial, empty, invalid)\n   241→- Mocked Docker client for unit tests\n   242→- Real Docker daemon for integration tests (marked `@pytest.mark.docker`)\n   243→\n   244→## Requirement Index\n   245→| ID | Section | Status |\n   246→|----|---------|--------|\n   247→| DS-F45 | Functional | Active |\n   248→| DS-F46 | Functional | Active |\n   249→| DS-F47 | Functional | Active |\n   250→| DS-F48 | Functional | Active |\n   251→| DS-F49 | Functional | Active |\n   252→| DS-F50 | Functional | Active |\n   253→| DS-F51 | Functional | Active |\n   254→| DS-F52 | Functional | Active |\n   255→| DS-F53 | Functional | Active |\n   256→| DS-F54 | Functional | Active |\n   257→| DS-F55 | Functional | Active |\n   258→| DS-NF10 | Non-Functional | Active |\n   259→| DS-NF11 | Non-Functional | Active |\n   260→| DS-NF12 | Non-Functional | Active |\n   261→\n   262→## Open Questions\n   263→- [ ] Does claudebox ship a pre-built image on GHCR, or must it always be built from a Dockerfile locally?\n   264→- [ ] Should the Dockerfile accept build-time UID/GID args, or should the container run as the claudebox default user?\n   265→- [ ] Where should the Dockerfile live: `vista/docker/Dockerfile`, `vista/.docker/Dockerfile`, or alongside the plugin manifest?\n   266→- [ ] Should there be an image version tag beyond \"latest\" for reproducibility?\n   267→- [ ] Is `network_enabled: false` implemented via `--network none` or `--network host`? What about DNS resolution?\n   268→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b3360bf-9ca7-4816-8cf1-455a270dc126","uuid":"b1a16d33-7968-41ce-9272-ec61846d418f","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista/.vista/features/docker-sandbox/specs/settings-and-image.md","content":"# Spec: Settings and Image\n\n## Overview\nDefines sandbox configuration in settings.json and manages Docker image auto-build from the claudebox base image for Vista-sandboxed execution.\n\n## Changelog\n| Date | ID | Change | Reason | Commit |\n|------|-----|--------|--------|--------|\n| 2026-02-12 | --- | Created | Initial spec generation | --- |\n\n## Parent JTBD\nProvide configurable sandbox settings and a ready-to-use Docker image so that sandboxed jobs can launch quickly with minimal user setup.\n\n## Scope\n**In Scope:**\n- SANDBOX_CONFIG section within settings.json schema\n- Configuration fields: image name, network mode, TTL, credential mount enable/disable\n- Docker image management: check existence, auto-build on first use, rebuild on demand\n- Claudebox base image integration and extension with Vista tooling\n- Image caching for fast subsequent job launches\n- Docker SDK connection validation (Layer 1 testing)\n- `GET /api/ralph/sandbox/status` response data (Docker installed, daemon running, image exists)\n- `POST /api/ralph/sandbox/build` handler logic\n\n**Out of Scope:**\n- Container creation and lifecycle (see container-lifecycle spec)\n- Credential mount path resolution (see credential-management spec)\n- Loop script generation (see bash-loop-generation spec)\n- RalphService integration logic (see ralph-sandbox-integration spec)\n- Docker Desktop installation or licensing\n- Custom Dockerfile authoring by users\n- Multi-image support (single image in v1)\n\n## Requirements\n### Functional\n1. **DS-F45:** settings.json SHALL support a `sandbox` section under the `ralph` configuration key with the following fields: `image` (str, default \"vista-ralph:latest\"), `network_enabled` (bool, default true), `ttl_seconds` (int, default 7200), `credential_mounts` (object).\n2. **DS-F46:** The `credential_mounts` config object SHALL contain entries for each credential type (`claude_auth`, `git_ssh`, `git_config`, `gh_cli`, `opencode`) each with an `enabled` (bool, default true) field.\n3. **DS-F47:** ContainerManager SHALL expose an `ensure_image(check_only=False)` method that checks if the configured image exists locally and, when `check_only=False` and image is missing, triggers an automatic build.\n4. **DS-F48:** The Docker image SHALL be built from the RchGrav/claudebox base image, extended with any Vista-specific tooling (e.g., git, curl) if not already present in claudebox.\n5. **DS-F49:** Image build progress SHALL be reported via a callback mechanism so callers (MCP tools, API) can surface \"Building Docker image...\" status to the user.\n6. **DS-F50:** The `POST /api/ralph/sandbox/build` endpoint SHALL force a rebuild of the Docker image even if one already exists, replacing the previous image.\n7. **DS-F51:** The `GET /api/ralph/sandbox/status` endpoint SHALL return a JSON object with `docker_installed` (bool), `daemon_running` (bool), `image_exists` (bool), and `image_name` (str).\n8. **DS-F52:** When the Docker Python SDK (`docker` package) is not installed, `docker_installed` SHALL be False and all sandbox operations SHALL raise a clear error: \"Docker SDK not installed. Run: pip install docker\".\n9. **DS-F53:** When the Docker daemon is not running, `daemon_running` SHALL be False and sandbox operations SHALL raise: \"Docker daemon is not running. Please start Docker Desktop.\"\n10. **DS-F54:** The image build SHALL use a Dockerfile stored within the Vista plugin directory (e.g., `vista/docker/Dockerfile`) that extends claudebox.\n11. **DS-F55:** Settings SHALL be validated on load: invalid `ttl_seconds` (negative or zero) SHALL be rejected, invalid image names SHALL be rejected.\n\n### Non-Functional\n1. **DS-NF10:** Image build time SHALL be under 5 minutes on a standard internet connection (first build, uncached).\n2. **DS-NF11:** Image existence check SHALL complete in under 1 second.\n3. **DS-NF12:** Settings defaults SHALL allow sandbox to work with zero configuration beyond having Docker installed.\n\n## User Workflows\n### Workflow: First Sandboxed Job (Image Auto-Build)\n**Actor:** User via Claude/MCP\n**Trigger:** First `ralph_start` with `sandbox=true` when no image exists\n**Steps:**\n1. RalphService calls ContainerManager.ensure_image()\n2. ContainerManager checks for image via Docker SDK: `client.images.get(\"vista-ralph:latest\")`\n3. Image not found: ContainerManager triggers build from Dockerfile\n4. Build progress reported to caller: \"Building Docker image (first time setup, ~2-5 minutes)...\"\n5. Build completes, image tagged as \"vista-ralph:latest\"\n6. ContainerManager returns success, job creation continues\n**Error Cases:**\n- Dockerfile not found: \"Vista Dockerfile not found at {path}. Plugin may be corrupted.\"\n- Build fails (network error): \"Image build failed: {build_log_tail}. Check network and retry with POST /api/ralph/sandbox/build\"\n- Build fails (Dockerfile error): \"Image build failed: {build_log_tail}. Please report this issue.\"\n- Claudebox base image not pullable: \"Cannot pull claudebox base image. Check Docker network access.\"\n\n### Workflow: Manual Image Rebuild\n**Actor:** User via dashboard or API\n**Trigger:** `POST /api/ralph/sandbox/build`\n**Steps:**\n1. API handler calls ContainerManager.ensure_image(force_rebuild=True)\n2. ContainerManager removes existing image (if any)\n3. ContainerManager builds fresh image from Dockerfile\n4. Returns build result with image ID and size\n**Error Cases:**\n- Image in use by running container: \"Cannot rebuild image while sandboxed jobs are running. Stop all sandboxed jobs first.\"\n\n### Workflow: Check Sandbox Readiness\n**Actor:** User or dashboard\n**Trigger:** `GET /api/ralph/sandbox/status`\n**Steps:**\n1. API handler attempts lazy import of `docker` package\n2. If import fails: return `{docker_installed: false, daemon_running: false, image_exists: false, image_name: \"vista-ralph:latest\"}`\n3. If import succeeds: attempt `docker.from_env().ping()`\n4. If ping fails: return `{docker_installed: true, daemon_running: false, image_exists: false, image_name: \"vista-ralph:latest\"}`\n5. If ping succeeds: check `client.images.get(image_name)`\n6. Return full status: `{docker_installed: true, daemon_running: true, image_exists: bool, image_name: \"vista-ralph:latest\"}`\n**Error Cases:**\n- Unexpected Docker API error: return `{docker_installed: true, daemon_running: false, ...}` with error detail\n\n### Workflow: User Customizes Sandbox Settings\n**Actor:** User editing settings.json\n**Trigger:** User wants to change TTL or disable network\n**Steps:**\n1. User opens settings.json, adds/modifies `ralph.sandbox` section\n2. Sets `network_enabled: false` for offline sandbox\n3. Sets `ttl_seconds: 3600` for shorter TTL\n4. Next sandboxed job uses updated settings\n**Error Cases:**\n- Invalid TTL (negative): validation rejects on settings load, uses default\n\n## Data Model\n**Entities:**\n- `SANDBOX_CONFIG`: `image` (str), `network_enabled` (bool), `ttl_seconds` (int), `credential_mounts` (dict of CredentialMountConfig)\n- `CredentialMountConfig`: `enabled` (bool)\n\n**Relationships:**\n- SETTINGS contains zero or one SANDBOX_CONFIG\n- SANDBOX_CONFIG contains zero or more CredentialMountConfig entries\n\n### Settings Schema Example\n```json\n{\n  \"ralph\": {\n    \"sandbox\": {\n      \"image\": \"vista-ralph:latest\",\n      \"network_enabled\": true,\n      \"ttl_seconds\": 7200,\n      \"credential_mounts\": {\n        \"claude_auth\": { \"enabled\": true },\n        \"git_ssh\": { \"enabled\": true },\n        \"git_config\": { \"enabled\": true },\n        \"gh_cli\": { \"enabled\": true },\n        \"opencode\": { \"enabled\": true }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Integration Points\n**Dependencies:**\n- Docker Python SDK (`docker` package, lazily imported)\n- Docker daemon (for image operations)\n- RchGrav/claudebox Docker image (base image pulled during build)\n- Vista plugin directory (for Dockerfile location)\n- settings.json loader (existing config infrastructure)\n\n**Provides to:**\n- ContainerManager: image name and sandbox configuration\n- CredentialMounter: credential_mounts enable/disable flags\n- ContainerManager: TTL and network settings\n- RalphService: sandbox config for job creation decisions\n- API routes: sandbox status and build endpoints\n\n## Technical Considerations\n### Architecture\n- SANDBOX_CONFIG parsed by existing settings loader with defaults for all fields\n- Dockerfile stored at `vista/docker/Dockerfile` (or `vista/docker/Dockerfile.sandbox`)\n- Image management methods on ContainerManager (or separate ImageManager if complexity warrants)\n- Docker client created lazily and cached for session lifetime\n\n### Patterns\n- Configuration with defaults: every field has a sensible default, sandbox works with zero config\n- Lazy loading: Docker SDK import deferred until first sandbox operation\n- Builder pattern potential: Dockerfile could be generated programmatically if claudebox extensions vary\n\n### Libraries/APIs\n- `docker.from_env()`: create Docker client from environment\n- `client.images.get(name)`: check image existence\n- `client.images.build(path, tag)`: build image from Dockerfile\n- `client.images.remove(name)`: remove image for rebuild\n- `client.ping()`: verify daemon connectivity\n\n### Dockerfile Structure (conceptual)\n```dockerfile\nFROM ghcr.io/rchgrav/claudebox:latest\n\n# Vista-specific additions (if needed)\nRUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y git curl && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*\n\n# Create non-root user matching host UID/GID (set at build or runtime)\nARG UID=1000\nARG GID=1000\nRUN groupadd -g $GID user && useradd -m -u $UID -g $GID user\n\nUSER user\nWORKDIR /workspace\n```\n\n## Related Diagrams\n- `arch/data-model.mmd` -- SETTINGS, SANDBOX_CONFIG, and CREDENTIAL_MOUNT entities\n- `arch/state-container.mmd` -- ImageCheck and Building states in container lifecycle\n- `arch/user-flow.mmd` -- Docker image check and auto-build decision flow\n- `arch/sequence-sandboxed-job.mmd` -- ensure_image() call in job creation sequence\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] DS-F45: settings.json supports `ralph.sandbox` with image, network_enabled, ttl_seconds, credential_mounts\n- [ ] DS-F45: Default values applied when sandbox section is absent: image=\"vista-ralph:latest\", network_enabled=true, ttl_seconds=7200\n- [ ] DS-F46: Each credential type has an `enabled` field defaulting to true\n- [ ] DS-F47: `ensure_image()` returns True when image exists without triggering build\n- [ ] DS-F47: `ensure_image()` triggers build when image missing and check_only=False\n- [ ] DS-F47: `ensure_image(check_only=True)` returns False when image missing, does not build\n- [ ] DS-F48: Built image is based on claudebox and tagged as configured image name\n- [ ] DS-F49: Build progress callback invoked during image build\n- [ ] DS-F50: `POST /api/ralph/sandbox/build` rebuilds image even when one exists\n- [ ] DS-F51: `GET /api/ralph/sandbox/status` returns correct JSON with all four fields\n- [ ] DS-F52: Docker SDK not installed produces clear error message with install instruction\n- [ ] DS-F53: Docker daemon not running produces clear error message mentioning Docker Desktop\n- [ ] DS-F54: Dockerfile exists at expected path within Vista plugin directory\n- [ ] DS-F55: Negative ttl_seconds rejected on settings validation\n- [ ] DS-NF10: Image build completes within 5 minutes on standard connection\n- [ ] DS-NF11: Image existence check completes under 1 second\n- [ ] DS-NF12: Sandbox works with only Docker installed and zero settings changes\n\n## Testing Strategy\n> Docker SDK connection testing (Layer 1) maps to this spec. Image management is part of ContainerManager TDD.\n\n**TDD Required:** Partial (settings validation is testable without Docker; Docker connection is integration)\n\n### Test Cases (from domain requirements Layer 1)\n#### Happy Path\n- `test_docker_sdk_import_succeeds`: `import docker` succeeds when package installed\n- `test_docker_daemon_ping_succeeds`: `docker.from_env().ping()` returns True (integration, requires Docker)\n- `test_image_exists_check`: `client.images.get(\"vista-ralph:latest\")` returns image object (integration)\n- `test_settings_defaults_applied`: Missing sandbox section produces correct defaults\n- `test_settings_custom_values`: Custom ttl_seconds and network_enabled parsed correctly\n- `test_credential_mounts_config_parsed`: All five credential types with enabled flags parsed\n- `test_sandbox_status_all_available`: Returns all true when Docker and image ready\n- `test_sandbox_status_no_docker`: Returns docker_installed=false\n\n#### Edge Cases\n- `test_settings_partial_sandbox_config`: Only image specified, rest default\n- `test_settings_partial_credential_mounts`: Only some credential types configured, rest default to enabled\n- `test_ensure_image_concurrent_calls`: Two simultaneous ensure_image calls do not duplicate builds\n- `test_rebuild_when_no_existing_image`: force_rebuild with no existing image just builds fresh\n\n#### Error Conditions\n- `test_docker_sdk_not_installed`: Import fails gracefully with clear error message\n- `test_docker_daemon_not_running`: Ping fails with clear error message\n- `test_image_build_network_failure`: Build fails with network error, returns useful message\n- `test_invalid_ttl_negative`: Negative ttl_seconds rejected at settings load\n- `test_invalid_ttl_zero`: Zero ttl_seconds rejected at settings load\n- `test_dockerfile_not_found`: Missing Dockerfile raises clear error with path\n\n### Test Data Requirements\n- Test settings.json with various sandbox configurations (full, partial, empty, invalid)\n- Mocked Docker client for unit tests\n- Real Docker daemon for integration tests (marked `@pytest.mark.docker`)\n\n## Requirement Index\n| ID | Section | Status |\n|----|---------|--------|\n| DS-F45 | Functional | Active |\n| DS-F46 | Functional | Active |\n| DS-F47 | Functional | Active |\n| DS-F48 | Functional | Active |\n| DS-F49 | Functional | Active |\n| DS-F50 | Functional | Active |\n| DS-F51 | Functional | Active |\n| DS-F52 | Functional | Active |\n| DS-F53 | Functional | Active |\n| DS-F54 | Functional | Active |\n| DS-F55 | Functional | Active |\n| DS-NF10 | Non-Functional | Active |\n| DS-NF11 | Non-Functional | Active |\n| DS-NF12 | Non-Functional | Active |\n\n## Open Questions\n- [ ] Does claudebox ship a pre-built image on GHCR, or must it always be built from a Dockerfile locally?\n- [ ] Should the Dockerfile accept build-time UID/GID args, or should the container run as the claudebox default user?\n- [ ] Where should the Dockerfile live: `vista/docker/Dockerfile`, `vista/.docker/Dockerfile`, or alongside the plugin manifest?\n- [ ] Should there be an image version tag beyond \"latest\" for reproducibility?\n- [ ] Is `network_enabled: false` implemented via `--network none` or `--network host`? What about DNS resolution?\n","numLines":268,"startLine":1,"totalLines":268}}}
