{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MsDUPghzAYDq9YmsmuvVTb","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Spec: Credential Management\n     2→\n     3→## Overview\n     4→Detects host credential directories, translates paths across operating systems, and generates read-only Docker bind mount specifications for container access.\n     5→\n     6→## Changelog\n     7→| Date | ID | Change | Reason | Commit |\n     8→|------|-----|--------|--------|--------|\n     9→| 2026-02-12 | --- | Created | Initial spec generation | --- |\n    10→\n    11→## Parent JTBD\n    12→Enable sandboxed agent loops to authenticate with external services (GitHub, Claude API, SSH remotes) by securely mounting host credentials into containers without write access.\n    13→\n    14→## Scope\n    15→**In Scope:**\n    16→- CredentialMounter class responsible for mount spec generation\n    17→- Detection of host credential directories on Windows, macOS, and Linux\n    18→- Path translation from host OS paths to Linux container paths\n    19→- Read-only mount mode enforcement for all credential mounts\n    20→- Graceful handling of missing credential directories (skip, do not fail)\n    21→- Configurable credential mount list via SANDBOX_CONFIG\n    22→- Support for individual credential mount enable/disable\n    23→\n    24→**Out of Scope:**\n    25→- Creating or managing credentials themselves\n    26→- Credential rotation or refresh inside containers\n    27→- Docker volume creation (uses bind mounts only)\n    28→- Network-based credential forwarding (e.g., SSH agent forwarding)\n    29→- Encrypting credentials at rest within containers\n    30→\n    31→## Requirements\n    32→### Functional\n    33→1. **DS-F12:** CredentialMounter SHALL detect and generate mount specs for these credential directories: `~/.claude/`, `~/.ssh/`, `~/.gitconfig`, `~/.config/gh/`, `~/.config/opencode/`.\n    34→2. **DS-F13:** All credential mounts SHALL use read-only mode (`ro`).\n    35→3. **DS-F14:** CredentialMounter SHALL resolve host credential paths using the correct home directory for the current OS: `%USERPROFILE%` on Windows, `$HOME` on macOS/Linux.\n    36→4. **DS-F15:** CredentialMounter SHALL translate host paths to Linux container paths using a fixed mapping: host `~/.claude/` -> container `/home/user/.claude/`, host `~/.ssh/` -> container `/home/user/.ssh/`, etc.\n    37→5. **DS-F16:** When a credential directory does not exist on the host, CredentialMounter SHALL skip that mount silently and continue with remaining mounts.\n    38→6. **DS-F17:** CredentialMounter SHALL accept a `credential_mounts` configuration (from SANDBOX_CONFIG) that allows enabling/disabling individual credential types.\n    39→7. **DS-F18:** CredentialMounter SHALL handle single-file credentials (e.g., `~/.gitconfig`) differently from directory credentials, using the correct Docker bind mount type.\n    40→8. **DS-F19:** CredentialMounter SHALL return mount specs as a list of `Mount` objects with `host_path`, `container_path`, `mode`, and `type` fields.\n    41→\n    42→### Non-Functional\n    43→1. **DS-NF4:** CredentialMounter SHALL be a pure logic class with no Docker SDK dependency, operating only on path resolution and mount spec generation.\n    44→2. **DS-NF5:** Path resolution SHALL work correctly regardless of whether the host uses forward slashes or backslashes.\n    45→\n    46→## User Workflows\n    47→### Workflow: Mount Specs Generated for Sandboxed Job\n    48→**Actor:** RalphService (internal caller)\n    49→**Trigger:** Sandboxed job creation needs credential mounts\n    50→**Steps:**\n    51→1. RalphService calls `CredentialMounter.get_mounts(host_os)` passing current platform\n    52→2. CredentialMounter reads SANDBOX_CONFIG for enabled credential types\n    53→3. For each enabled credential type, resolves host path using OS-appropriate home directory\n    54→4. Checks if host path exists on filesystem\n    55→5. If exists: generates Mount spec with host path, container target path, and `ro` mode\n    56→6. If missing: logs debug message, skips this mount\n    57→7. Returns list of Mount specs to RalphService\n    58→8. RalphService passes mount specs to ContainerManager for container creation\n    59→**Error Cases:**\n    60→- Home directory not resolvable: raise configuration error (should never happen in practice)\n    61→- All credential directories missing: return empty list (container runs without credentials)\n    62→\n    63→### Workflow: User Disables Specific Credential Mount\n    64→**Actor:** User editing settings.json\n    65→**Trigger:** User wants to exclude SSH keys from container\n    66→**Steps:**\n    67→1. User sets `credential_mounts.git_ssh.enabled = false` in settings.json\n    68→2. Next sandboxed job creation: CredentialMounter reads config, skips `~/.ssh/` mount\n    69→3. Container created without SSH key access\n    70→**Error Cases:**\n    71→- Invalid credential mount name in config: ignored, does not affect other mounts\n    72→\n    73→## Data Model\n    74→**Entities:**\n    75→- `CredentialMount` (config): `name` (str: \"claude_auth\", \"git_ssh\", \"git_config\", \"gh_cli\", \"opencode\"), `host_path` (str, OS-specific), `container_path` (str, Linux), `mode` (\"ro\"), `enabled` (bool)\n    76→- `Mount` (runtime): `host_path` (str, resolved absolute), `container_path` (str), `mode` (\"ro\"), `type` (\"credential\")\n    77→\n    78→**Relationships:**\n    79→- SANDBOX_CONFIG has one or more CredentialMount definitions\n    80→- CredentialMounter produces zero or more Mount specs per invocation\n    81→\n    82→## Integration Points\n    83→**Dependencies:**\n    84→- Host filesystem (to check credential directory existence)\n    85→- SANDBOX_CONFIG from settings (for credential mount definitions and enable/disable)\n    86→- `platform` module (for OS detection)\n    87→- `pathlib.Path` (for cross-platform path resolution)\n    88→\n    89→**Provides to:**\n    90→- ContainerManager: mount specs included in `create_container()` call\n    91→- RalphService: intermediary caller\n    92→\n    93→## Technical Considerations\n    94→### Architecture\n    95→- CredentialMounter is a standalone class in `server/services/credential_mounter.py`\n    96→- No Docker SDK dependency -- pure path logic and filesystem checks\n    97→- Default credential mount definitions hardcoded with config overrides\n    98→\n    99→### Patterns\n   100→- Registry pattern: default credential types registered internally, overridable via config\n   101→- Null object pattern: missing credentials produce empty mount list, not errors\n   102→\n   103→### Libraries/APIs\n   104→- `pathlib.Path.home()` for cross-platform home directory resolution\n   105→- `pathlib.Path.exists()` for credential directory detection\n   106→- `platform.system()` for OS identification\n   107→- `os.environ.get(\"USERPROFILE\")` as Windows fallback\n   108→\n   109→### Credential Path Mapping Table\n   110→\n   111→| Credential | Host Path (Windows) | Host Path (macOS/Linux) | Container Path |\n   112→|------------|-------------------|------------------------|----------------|\n   113→| Claude auth | `%USERPROFILE%\\.claude\\` | `~/.claude/` | `/home/user/.claude/` |\n   114→| SSH keys | `%USERPROFILE%\\.ssh\\` | `~/.ssh/` | `/home/user/.ssh/` |\n   115→| Git config | `%USERPROFILE%\\.gitconfig` | `~/.gitconfig` | `/home/user/.gitconfig` |\n   116→| GitHub CLI | `%USERPROFILE%\\.config\\gh\\` | `~/.config/gh/` | `/home/user/.config/gh/` |\n   117→| OpenCode | `%USERPROFILE%\\.config\\opencode\\` | `~/.config/opencode/` | `/home/user/.config/opencode/` |\n   118→\n   119→## Related Diagrams\n   120→- `arch/data-model.mmd` -- CREDENTIAL_MOUNT entity and relationship to SANDBOX_CONFIG\n   121→- `arch/system-architecture.mmd` -- CredentialMounter component within host services\n   122→- `arch/sequence-sandboxed-job.mmd` -- CredentialMounter called during job creation sequence\n   123→\n   124→## Acceptance Criteria\n   125→- [ ] DS-F12: Mount specs generated for all five credential directories when all exist on host\n   126→- [ ] DS-F13: Every mount spec in the returned list has `mode=\"ro\"`\n   127→- [ ] DS-F14: On Windows, host paths resolve using `%USERPROFILE%`; on macOS/Linux, using `$HOME`\n   128→- [ ] DS-F15: Container paths follow `/home/user/` prefix convention for all credential types\n   129→- [ ] DS-F16: Missing `~/.ssh/` on host produces mount list without SSH entry, no error raised\n   130→- [ ] DS-F16: All credential directories missing produces empty mount list, no error raised\n   131→- [ ] DS-F17: Setting `git_ssh.enabled=false` in config excludes SSH mount from results\n   132→- [ ] DS-F18: `~/.gitconfig` (file) and `~/.ssh/` (directory) produce correct bind mount types\n   133→- [ ] DS-F19: Each mount spec has all four fields: host_path, container_path, mode, type\n   134→\n   135→## Testing Strategy\n   136→> CredentialMounter is a TDD-flagged component\n   137→\n   138→**TDD Required:** Yes\n   139→**TDD Diagrams:** N/A (pure logic, state diagram not applicable)\n   140→\n   141→### Test Cases (from domain requirements Layer 3)\n   142→#### Happy Path\n   143→- `test_all_credentials_exist_all_mounted`: All 5 credential dirs exist, 5 mount specs returned\n   144→- `test_mount_mode_always_ro`: Every returned mount has mode=\"ro\"\n   145→- `test_mount_type_always_credential`: Every returned mount has type=\"credential\"\n   146→- `test_windows_paths_resolved_correctly`: On Windows (mocked), host paths use USERPROFILE\n   147→- `test_linux_paths_resolved_correctly`: On Linux (mocked), host paths use HOME\n   148→- `test_macos_paths_resolved_correctly`: On macOS (mocked), host paths use HOME\n   149→- `test_container_paths_use_home_user_prefix`: All container paths start with `/home/user/`\n   150→- `test_gitconfig_file_mount`: `~/.gitconfig` produces file bind mount, not directory mount\n   151→- `test_ssh_directory_mount`: `~/.ssh/` produces directory bind mount\n   152→\n   153→#### Edge Cases\n   154→- `test_no_credentials_exist`: All 5 missing, returns empty list, no error\n   155→- `test_partial_credentials`: Only `~/.claude/` and `~/.ssh/` exist, returns 2 mount specs\n   156→- `test_disabled_credential_skipped`: `git_ssh.enabled=false` excludes SSH even if dir exists\n   157→- `test_all_credentials_disabled`: All disabled in config, returns empty list\n   158→- `test_windows_backslash_paths`: Windows paths with backslashes handled correctly\n   159→- `test_symlinked_credential_dir`: Symlinked `~/.ssh` resolves and mounts correctly\n   160→\n   161→#### Error Conditions\n   162→- `test_home_dir_not_resolvable`: Raises clear configuration error (mocked scenario)\n   163→- `test_invalid_credential_name_in_config`: Unknown names in config ignored, valid ones processed\n   164→\n   165→### Test Data Requirements\n   166→- Mocked `platform.system()` returning \"Windows\", \"Darwin\", \"Linux\"\n   167→- Mocked `Path.home()` returning OS-appropriate paths\n   168→- Mocked `Path.exists()` returning True/False per credential directory\n   169→- Test SANDBOX_CONFIG with various credential enable/disable combinations\n   170→\n   171→## Requirement Index\n   172→| ID | Section | Status |\n   173→|----|---------|--------|\n   174→| DS-F12 | Functional | Active |\n   175→| DS-F13 | Functional | Active |\n   176→| DS-F14 | Functional | Active |\n   177→| DS-F15 | Functional | Active |\n   178→| DS-F16 | Functional | Active |\n   179→| DS-F17 | Functional | Active |\n   180→| DS-F18 | Functional | Active |\n   181→| DS-F19 | Functional | Active |\n   182→| DS-NF4 | Non-Functional | Active |\n   183→| DS-NF5 | Non-Functional | Active |\n   184→\n   185→## Open Questions\n   186→- [ ] Should the container user be `user` (matching claudebox base image) or configurable?\n   187→- [ ] Should UID/GID mapping be handled here or in ContainerManager? Domain requirements specify \"UID/GID matching host user.\"\n   188→- [ ] Is SSH agent forwarding needed in v1, or is key file mounting sufficient?\n   189→- [ ] Should `~/.config/opencode/` path vary by OS (e.g., `%APPDATA%\\opencode\\` on Windows)?\n   190→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b3360bf-9ca7-4816-8cf1-455a270dc126","uuid":"fb028b2a-66f1-4611-815b-2b29edd5d0fd","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista/.vista/features/docker-sandbox/specs/credential-management.md","content":"# Spec: Credential Management\n\n## Overview\nDetects host credential directories, translates paths across operating systems, and generates read-only Docker bind mount specifications for container access.\n\n## Changelog\n| Date | ID | Change | Reason | Commit |\n|------|-----|--------|--------|--------|\n| 2026-02-12 | --- | Created | Initial spec generation | --- |\n\n## Parent JTBD\nEnable sandboxed agent loops to authenticate with external services (GitHub, Claude API, SSH remotes) by securely mounting host credentials into containers without write access.\n\n## Scope\n**In Scope:**\n- CredentialMounter class responsible for mount spec generation\n- Detection of host credential directories on Windows, macOS, and Linux\n- Path translation from host OS paths to Linux container paths\n- Read-only mount mode enforcement for all credential mounts\n- Graceful handling of missing credential directories (skip, do not fail)\n- Configurable credential mount list via SANDBOX_CONFIG\n- Support for individual credential mount enable/disable\n\n**Out of Scope:**\n- Creating or managing credentials themselves\n- Credential rotation or refresh inside containers\n- Docker volume creation (uses bind mounts only)\n- Network-based credential forwarding (e.g., SSH agent forwarding)\n- Encrypting credentials at rest within containers\n\n## Requirements\n### Functional\n1. **DS-F12:** CredentialMounter SHALL detect and generate mount specs for these credential directories: `~/.claude/`, `~/.ssh/`, `~/.gitconfig`, `~/.config/gh/`, `~/.config/opencode/`.\n2. **DS-F13:** All credential mounts SHALL use read-only mode (`ro`).\n3. **DS-F14:** CredentialMounter SHALL resolve host credential paths using the correct home directory for the current OS: `%USERPROFILE%` on Windows, `$HOME` on macOS/Linux.\n4. **DS-F15:** CredentialMounter SHALL translate host paths to Linux container paths using a fixed mapping: host `~/.claude/` -> container `/home/user/.claude/`, host `~/.ssh/` -> container `/home/user/.ssh/`, etc.\n5. **DS-F16:** When a credential directory does not exist on the host, CredentialMounter SHALL skip that mount silently and continue with remaining mounts.\n6. **DS-F17:** CredentialMounter SHALL accept a `credential_mounts` configuration (from SANDBOX_CONFIG) that allows enabling/disabling individual credential types.\n7. **DS-F18:** CredentialMounter SHALL handle single-file credentials (e.g., `~/.gitconfig`) differently from directory credentials, using the correct Docker bind mount type.\n8. **DS-F19:** CredentialMounter SHALL return mount specs as a list of `Mount` objects with `host_path`, `container_path`, `mode`, and `type` fields.\n\n### Non-Functional\n1. **DS-NF4:** CredentialMounter SHALL be a pure logic class with no Docker SDK dependency, operating only on path resolution and mount spec generation.\n2. **DS-NF5:** Path resolution SHALL work correctly regardless of whether the host uses forward slashes or backslashes.\n\n## User Workflows\n### Workflow: Mount Specs Generated for Sandboxed Job\n**Actor:** RalphService (internal caller)\n**Trigger:** Sandboxed job creation needs credential mounts\n**Steps:**\n1. RalphService calls `CredentialMounter.get_mounts(host_os)` passing current platform\n2. CredentialMounter reads SANDBOX_CONFIG for enabled credential types\n3. For each enabled credential type, resolves host path using OS-appropriate home directory\n4. Checks if host path exists on filesystem\n5. If exists: generates Mount spec with host path, container target path, and `ro` mode\n6. If missing: logs debug message, skips this mount\n7. Returns list of Mount specs to RalphService\n8. RalphService passes mount specs to ContainerManager for container creation\n**Error Cases:**\n- Home directory not resolvable: raise configuration error (should never happen in practice)\n- All credential directories missing: return empty list (container runs without credentials)\n\n### Workflow: User Disables Specific Credential Mount\n**Actor:** User editing settings.json\n**Trigger:** User wants to exclude SSH keys from container\n**Steps:**\n1. User sets `credential_mounts.git_ssh.enabled = false` in settings.json\n2. Next sandboxed job creation: CredentialMounter reads config, skips `~/.ssh/` mount\n3. Container created without SSH key access\n**Error Cases:**\n- Invalid credential mount name in config: ignored, does not affect other mounts\n\n## Data Model\n**Entities:**\n- `CredentialMount` (config): `name` (str: \"claude_auth\", \"git_ssh\", \"git_config\", \"gh_cli\", \"opencode\"), `host_path` (str, OS-specific), `container_path` (str, Linux), `mode` (\"ro\"), `enabled` (bool)\n- `Mount` (runtime): `host_path` (str, resolved absolute), `container_path` (str), `mode` (\"ro\"), `type` (\"credential\")\n\n**Relationships:**\n- SANDBOX_CONFIG has one or more CredentialMount definitions\n- CredentialMounter produces zero or more Mount specs per invocation\n\n## Integration Points\n**Dependencies:**\n- Host filesystem (to check credential directory existence)\n- SANDBOX_CONFIG from settings (for credential mount definitions and enable/disable)\n- `platform` module (for OS detection)\n- `pathlib.Path` (for cross-platform path resolution)\n\n**Provides to:**\n- ContainerManager: mount specs included in `create_container()` call\n- RalphService: intermediary caller\n\n## Technical Considerations\n### Architecture\n- CredentialMounter is a standalone class in `server/services/credential_mounter.py`\n- No Docker SDK dependency -- pure path logic and filesystem checks\n- Default credential mount definitions hardcoded with config overrides\n\n### Patterns\n- Registry pattern: default credential types registered internally, overridable via config\n- Null object pattern: missing credentials produce empty mount list, not errors\n\n### Libraries/APIs\n- `pathlib.Path.home()` for cross-platform home directory resolution\n- `pathlib.Path.exists()` for credential directory detection\n- `platform.system()` for OS identification\n- `os.environ.get(\"USERPROFILE\")` as Windows fallback\n\n### Credential Path Mapping Table\n\n| Credential | Host Path (Windows) | Host Path (macOS/Linux) | Container Path |\n|------------|-------------------|------------------------|----------------|\n| Claude auth | `%USERPROFILE%\\.claude\\` | `~/.claude/` | `/home/user/.claude/` |\n| SSH keys | `%USERPROFILE%\\.ssh\\` | `~/.ssh/` | `/home/user/.ssh/` |\n| Git config | `%USERPROFILE%\\.gitconfig` | `~/.gitconfig` | `/home/user/.gitconfig` |\n| GitHub CLI | `%USERPROFILE%\\.config\\gh\\` | `~/.config/gh/` | `/home/user/.config/gh/` |\n| OpenCode | `%USERPROFILE%\\.config\\opencode\\` | `~/.config/opencode/` | `/home/user/.config/opencode/` |\n\n## Related Diagrams\n- `arch/data-model.mmd` -- CREDENTIAL_MOUNT entity and relationship to SANDBOX_CONFIG\n- `arch/system-architecture.mmd` -- CredentialMounter component within host services\n- `arch/sequence-sandboxed-job.mmd` -- CredentialMounter called during job creation sequence\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] DS-F12: Mount specs generated for all five credential directories when all exist on host\n- [ ] DS-F13: Every mount spec in the returned list has `mode=\"ro\"`\n- [ ] DS-F14: On Windows, host paths resolve using `%USERPROFILE%`; on macOS/Linux, using `$HOME`\n- [ ] DS-F15: Container paths follow `/home/user/` prefix convention for all credential types\n- [ ] DS-F16: Missing `~/.ssh/` on host produces mount list without SSH entry, no error raised\n- [ ] DS-F16: All credential directories missing produces empty mount list, no error raised\n- [ ] DS-F17: Setting `git_ssh.enabled=false` in config excludes SSH mount from results\n- [ ] DS-F18: `~/.gitconfig` (file) and `~/.ssh/` (directory) produce correct bind mount types\n- [ ] DS-F19: Each mount spec has all four fields: host_path, container_path, mode, type\n\n## Testing Strategy\n> CredentialMounter is a TDD-flagged component\n\n**TDD Required:** Yes\n**TDD Diagrams:** N/A (pure logic, state diagram not applicable)\n\n### Test Cases (from domain requirements Layer 3)\n#### Happy Path\n- `test_all_credentials_exist_all_mounted`: All 5 credential dirs exist, 5 mount specs returned\n- `test_mount_mode_always_ro`: Every returned mount has mode=\"ro\"\n- `test_mount_type_always_credential`: Every returned mount has type=\"credential\"\n- `test_windows_paths_resolved_correctly`: On Windows (mocked), host paths use USERPROFILE\n- `test_linux_paths_resolved_correctly`: On Linux (mocked), host paths use HOME\n- `test_macos_paths_resolved_correctly`: On macOS (mocked), host paths use HOME\n- `test_container_paths_use_home_user_prefix`: All container paths start with `/home/user/`\n- `test_gitconfig_file_mount`: `~/.gitconfig` produces file bind mount, not directory mount\n- `test_ssh_directory_mount`: `~/.ssh/` produces directory bind mount\n\n#### Edge Cases\n- `test_no_credentials_exist`: All 5 missing, returns empty list, no error\n- `test_partial_credentials`: Only `~/.claude/` and `~/.ssh/` exist, returns 2 mount specs\n- `test_disabled_credential_skipped`: `git_ssh.enabled=false` excludes SSH even if dir exists\n- `test_all_credentials_disabled`: All disabled in config, returns empty list\n- `test_windows_backslash_paths`: Windows paths with backslashes handled correctly\n- `test_symlinked_credential_dir`: Symlinked `~/.ssh` resolves and mounts correctly\n\n#### Error Conditions\n- `test_home_dir_not_resolvable`: Raises clear configuration error (mocked scenario)\n- `test_invalid_credential_name_in_config`: Unknown names in config ignored, valid ones processed\n\n### Test Data Requirements\n- Mocked `platform.system()` returning \"Windows\", \"Darwin\", \"Linux\"\n- Mocked `Path.home()` returning OS-appropriate paths\n- Mocked `Path.exists()` returning True/False per credential directory\n- Test SANDBOX_CONFIG with various credential enable/disable combinations\n\n## Requirement Index\n| ID | Section | Status |\n|----|---------|--------|\n| DS-F12 | Functional | Active |\n| DS-F13 | Functional | Active |\n| DS-F14 | Functional | Active |\n| DS-F15 | Functional | Active |\n| DS-F16 | Functional | Active |\n| DS-F17 | Functional | Active |\n| DS-F18 | Functional | Active |\n| DS-F19 | Functional | Active |\n| DS-NF4 | Non-Functional | Active |\n| DS-NF5 | Non-Functional | Active |\n\n## Open Questions\n- [ ] Should the container user be `user` (matching claudebox base image) or configurable?\n- [ ] Should UID/GID mapping be handled here or in ContainerManager? Domain requirements specify \"UID/GID matching host user.\"\n- [ ] Is SSH agent forwarding needed in v1, or is key file mounting sufficient?\n- [ ] Should `~/.config/opencode/` path vary by OS (e.g., `%APPDATA%\\opencode\\` on Windows)?\n","numLines":190,"startLine":1,"totalLines":190}}}
